translate chinese strings:

    old "Yes, but only in the abstract sense. It's good to have friends in high places."
    new "Yes, but only in the abstract sense. It's good to have friends in high places.\n是的，但只是抽象意义上的。在高处有朋友是件好事。"

    old "After all, you do directly serve the council. That makes you quite powerful, does it not?"
    new "After all, you do directly serve the council. That makes you quite powerful, does it not?\n毕竟，你确实直接为议会效力。这让你相当有权势，不是吗？"

    old "I suppose I am quite powerful. I do speak directly to members of the council regularly."
    new "I suppose I am quite powerful. I do speak directly to members of the council regularly.\n我想我确实相当有权势。我经常直接与议会成员交谈。"

    old "It's one thing to speak to the council. Anyone can make an appeal to the council. The thing that gives you power is that the council relies on you."
    new "It's one thing to speak to the council. Anyone can make an appeal to the council. The thing that gives you power is that the council relies on you.\n向议会陈情是一回事，任何人都可以向议会申诉。真正赋予你权力的是，议会依赖你。"

    old "Yes, and they do."
    new "Yes, and they do.\n是的，他们确实依赖我。"

    old "There's an interesting thing about service. A master may have control of a serf who works the master's land, who harvests the grain and forms it into bread for the master to eat.. But if the serf decides to walk away, and the master has no one else to feed him, then who is it that really holds the power in that relationship?"
    new "There's an interesting thing about service. A master may have control of a serf who works the master's land, who harvests the grain and forms it into bread for the master to eat.. But if the serf decides to walk away, and the master has no one else to feed him, then who is it that really holds the power in that relationship?\n效劳这件事有个有趣的地方。主人或许能支配在他土地上劳作的农奴，那农奴收割谷物，做成面包供主人食用……但如果农奴决定一走了之，而主人身边再没有别的人来供养他，那么这段关系里真正握有权力的是谁呢？"

    old "In fact, servants tend to be the most useful of friends to have, because people so often underestimate how important they are."
    new "In fact, servants tend to be the most useful of friends to have, because people so often underestimate how important they are.\n事实上，仆人往往是最有用的朋友，因为人们总是低估他们的重要性。"

    old "I'm not powerful at all. As you said, I serve the council. That means the orders flow in one direction, from them to me. I can't very well tell the council what to do."
    new "I'm not powerful at all. As you said, I serve the council. That means the orders flow in one direction, from them to me. I can't very well tell the council what to do.\n我一点权力都没有。正如你说的，我为议会效力。这意味着命令只朝一个方向流动，从他们到我。我总不能反过来吩咐议会该怎么做。"

    old "But the council has made decisions based on information you've given them, have they not? As I understand it, Grimoire is now preparing for war. That's partly due to your actions and your scouting."
    new "But the council has made decisions based on information you've given them, have they not? As I understand it, Grimoire is now preparing for war. That's partly due to your actions and your scouting.\n但议会一直是根据你提供的情报来做决定的，不是吗？据我所知，Grimoire 如今正在备战。这在一定程度上要归功于你的行动和侦察。"

    old "Had you given them different information, they might be behaving very differently right now. You do serve the council, yes, but you hold more power and influence than you might think."
    new "Had you given them different information, they might be behaving very differently right now. You do serve the council, yes, but you hold more power and influence than you might think.\n假如你当初给了他们不同的情报，他们此刻的行为可能截然不同。你确实为议会效力，没错，但你握有的权力和影响力比你以为的更大。"

    old "While the council holds direct authority over you, I think that the council needs you more than you need the council. But you both benefit from that arrangement, so the truth is that you may be able to call the council's members your peers and be more accurate than most people might think."
    new "While the council holds direct authority over you, I think that the council needs you more than you need the council. But you both benefit from that arrangement, so the truth is that you may be able to call the council's members your peers and be more accurate than most people might think.\n虽然议会对你有直接权威，但我认为议会更需要你，胜过你需要议会。不过这段安排让双方都受益，所以事实是，你或许可以把议会成员称作你的同侪，而且这比大多数人想象得更准确。"

    old "The more transactional things become, the more equal they tend to become. I think that may be the root of why I became a merchant. It's because I value equality so much."
    new "The more transactional things become, the more equal they tend to become. I think that may be the root of why I became a merchant. It's because I value equality so much.\n事情越带有交易性质，往往就越趋于平等。我想这可能就是我成为商人的根源——因为我太看重平等了。"

    old "How has becoming a merchant made you 'more equal?'"
    new "How has becoming a merchant made you 'more equal?'\n成为商人怎么让你‘更加平等’了？"

    old "[protag], surely you understand what it means to be a merchant."
    new "[protag], surely you understand what it means to be a merchant.\n[protag]，你当然明白当商人意味着什么。"

    old "In fact, as I understand it, you have a background in mercantilism yourself."
    new "In fact, as I understand it, you have a background in mercantilism yourself.\n事实上，据我所知，你自己就有经商的背景。"

    old "Yes, that's true. Before I became responsible for ridding the world of vampires, I was a trader of goods."
    new "Yes, that's true. Before I became responsible for ridding the world of vampires, I was a trader of goods.\n是的，没错。在我肩负起清除世间 Vampires 的职责之前，我是个商品商人。"

    old "You're a person who exchanges goods."
    new "You're a person who exchanges goods.\n你是个交换商品的人。"

    old "Most people think that merchants are in the business of moving wealth around. Some times it's in the form of goods, sometimes it's in the form of money which can be exchanged for goods. But even when money is involved, fundamentally, merchants are in the business of what we call trade."
    new "Most people think that merchants are in the business of moving wealth around. Some times it's in the form of goods, sometimes it's in the form of money which can be exchanged for goods. But even when money is involved, fundamentally, merchants are in the business of what we call trade.\n大多数人以为，商人做的就是把财富挪来挪去的生意。有时以商品的形式，有时以金钱的形式——金钱又可以换回商品。但即便牵扯到钱，从根本上说，商人做的还是我们所说的‘贸易’。"

    old "I love that word. 'Trade.' What does it mean? Trade, when conducted with mutual consent, is practically by definition mutually beneficial. After all, each of the parties wouldn't agree to the trade if it didn't benefit them in some way. So both parties need to feel like they are coming out ahead."
    new "I love that word. 'Trade.' What does it mean? Trade, when conducted with mutual consent, is practically by definition mutually beneficial. After all, each of the parties wouldn't agree to the trade if it didn't benefit them in some way. So both parties need to feel like they are coming out ahead.\n我喜欢这个词。‘贸易’。它是什么意思？在双方同意的前提下进行的贸易，几乎从定义上就是互惠互利的。毕竟，如果一笔交易不能给各方带来某种好处，哪一方都不会同意。所以双方都得觉得自己占了便宜。"

    old "When a successful transaction happens, both parties are made to feel like they are better off than when they started. They need to feel like they have gained value. In a certain sense, any trade makes both parties wealthier. By facilitating trade, merchants don't just move the wealth around. They increase it."
    new "When a successful transaction happens, both parties are made to feel like they are better off than when they started. They need to feel like they have gained value. In a certain sense, any trade makes both parties wealthier. By facilitating trade, merchants don't just move the wealth around. They increase it.\n一笔成功的交易达成时，双方都会觉得自己比开始时境况更好了。他们需要觉得自己得到了价值。从某种意义上说，任何交易都让双方变得更富有。通过促成贸易，商人不是在挪动财富，而是在增加财富。"

    old "That sounds counter-intuitive. If I have five apples and exchange them for five loaves of bread, at both the beginning and the end of the transaction, there are still a total of five loaves and five apples. The trade hasn't changed the value of those goods, so how can you say that there has been a wealth increase?"
    new "That sounds counter-intuitive. If I have five apples and exchange them for five loaves of bread, at both the beginning and the end of the transaction, there are still a total of five loaves and five apples. The trade hasn't changed the value of those goods, so how can you say that there has been a wealth increase?\n这听起来有违直觉。如果我有五个苹果，用它们换五条面包，那在这笔交易的起点和终点，总共都还是五条面包加五个苹果。交易并没有改变这些货物的价值，那你凭什么说财富增加了？"

    old "Ah, but suppose you love bread and loathe apples, while your neighbor hates bread and loves apples. At the beginning of the transaction, you are both relatively unhappy. After the transaction, both of you walk away with something that delights you. Hasn't the wealth in that situation increased?"
    new "Ah, but suppose you love bread and loathe apples, while your neighbor hates bread and loves apples. At the beginning of the transaction, you are both relatively unhappy. After the transaction, both of you walk away with something that delights you. Hasn't the wealth in that situation increased?\n啊，但假设你爱吃面包、讨厌苹果，而你的邻居讨厌面包、爱吃苹果。交易开始前，你俩都挺不高兴。交易结束后，你俩都带着让自己开心的东西离开。那种情形下，财富难道没有增加吗？"

    old "Yes. We're both better off than where we started. So in a sense, we are both 'wealthier', in the sense of being more well-off."
    new "Yes. We're both better off than where we started. So in a sense, we are both 'wealthier', in the sense of being more well-off.\n对。我们俩都比开始时境况更好了。所以从某种意义上说，我们俩都‘更富有’了，也就是日子过得更宽裕了。"

    old "I'm so glad you understand. You'd be surprised how rare it is to find someone who actually understands the concept of wealth in this way."
    new "I'm so glad you understand. You'd be surprised how rare it is to find someone who actually understands the concept of wealth in this way.\n我很高兴你能理解。能找到一个真正这样理解财富概念的人，实在难得，你会为此惊讶的。"

    old "No. Wealth is finite, and moving things around doesn't increase it. You can't increase the amount of gold that exists in the world, for example. You can only redistribute it."
    new "No. Wealth is finite, and moving things around doesn't increase it. You can't increase the amount of gold that exists in the world, for example. You can only redistribute it.\n不。财富是有限的，把东西挪来挪去不会让它变多。比如说，你无法增加世上现存黄金的总量，只能重新分配它。"

    old "But you can mine gold from the ground."
    new "But you can mine gold from the ground.\n但你可以从地里挖出黄金。"

    old "Yes, but that doesn't actually create more gold. It just relocates the gold from below the ground to existing in your coffers. That's just another form of redistributing wealth. As you get richer, the ground, in an abstract sense, grows poorer. The land that you mined the gold from becomes less valuable than it would have been before you took the gold."
    new "Yes, but that doesn't actually create more gold. It just relocates the gold from below the ground to existing in your coffers. That's just another form of redistributing wealth. As you get richer, the ground, in an abstract sense, grows poorer. The land that you mined the gold from becomes less valuable than it would have been before you took the gold.\n是的，但那并不会真的变出更多黄金。它只是把黄金从地下挪到了你的金库里。那不过是重新分配财富的另一种形式罢了。随着你越来越富有，从抽象意义上说，那片土地就越来越贫穷。你开采出黄金的那块地，价值比开采之前更低了。"

    old "But gold isn't really what wealth is. It just represents value, just like money. You agree with me there, correct? Suppose there was a land where everyone lived in luxury, everyone had bountiful supplies of food and wine and fine pieces of art. We'd say that they were wealthy, even if they had no gold. You can at least agree with that, can't you?"
    new "But gold isn't really what wealth is. It just represents value, just like money. You agree with me there, correct? Suppose there was a land where everyone lived in luxury, everyone had bountiful supplies of food and wine and fine pieces of art. We'd say that they were wealthy, even if they had no gold. You can at least agree with that, can't you?\n但黄金并非财富本身。它只是价值的象征，跟金钱一样。这一点你同意我吧？假设有片土地，人人都过着奢华的生活，人人都坐拥充裕的食物、美酒和精美的艺术品。即便他们一块黄金都没有，我们也会说他们很富有。这一点你至少能同意吧？"

    old "Things like money and gold are not wealth. Now, in a way, they represent wealth. They are useful because they can be exchanged for things that you want. But really, they are just a measure of potential wealth."
    new "Things like money and gold are not wealth. Now, in a way, they represent wealth. They are useful because they can be exchanged for things that you want. But really, they are just a measure of potential wealth.\n金钱和黄金这类东西并不是财富。当然，从某种意义上说，它们象征着财富。它们有用，是因为能拿来换取你想要的东西。但说到底，它们只是潜在财富的一种度量。"

    old "Wealth is things that people want. Think about what a baker does. A baker buys ingredients, bakes a loaf of bread, and then sells the bread for more than he purchased the ingredients. He profits. How did he profit?"
    new "Wealth is things that people want. Think about what a baker does. A baker buys ingredients, bakes a loaf of bread, and then sells the bread for more than he purchased the ingredients. He profits. How did he profit?\n财富是人们想要的东西。想想面包师的做法。面包师买来原料，烤出一条面包，再以高于进价的价格把面包卖出去。他赚了钱。他是怎么赚钱的？"

    old "He literally created wealth by taking a pile of ingredients, something that people consider less useful, and transforming it into a loaf of bread, something that anyone can consider to be of value. And furthermore, the value of that loaf of bread may change on the following day, because value is not an immutable property of anything."
    new "He literally created wealth by taking a pile of ingredients, something that people consider less useful, and transforming it into a loaf of bread, something that anyone can consider to be of value. And furthermore, the value of that loaf of bread may change on the following day, because value is not an immutable property of anything.\n他确实创造了财富——把一堆人们认为用处不大的原料，变成了一条人人都会认为有价值的面包。而且，那条面包的价值第二天可能就会变，因为价值不是任何事物固有不变的属性。"

    old "Wealth can be created."
    new "Wealth can be created.\n财富是可以被创造出来的。"

    old "I'm so glad you understand. You'd be surprised how rare it is to find someone who actually understands the concept of wealth."
    new "I'm so glad you understand. You'd be surprised how rare it is to find someone who actually understands the concept of wealth.\n我很高兴你能理解。能找到一个真正理解财富概念的人，实在难得，你会为此惊讶的。"

    old "For example, on one of my first business ventures, I physically transported furs from GrandTree to Triberg. I knew that the trappers near GrandTree and the Great Forest had enjoyed a particularly bountiful season, and that meant that anyone near to GrandTree could enjoy a surplus of available furs."
    new "For example, on one of my first business ventures, I physically transported furs from GrandTree to Triberg. I knew that the trappers near GrandTree and the Great Forest had enjoyed a particularly bountiful season, and that meant that anyone near to GrandTree could enjoy a surplus of available furs.\n举个例子，在我最早的几桩生意里，有一桩是我亲自把毛皮从 GrandTree 运到 Triberg。我得知 GrandTree 和 Great Forest 一带的猎户度过了格外丰饶的一季，这意味着住在 GrandTree 附近的人都能享受毛皮过剩的好处。"

    old "Now, as luck would have it, Triberg was in for an especially harsh weather that year. Not too harsh, understand, as Triberg has always had moderate climate, but cold enough that for the first time many people were looking to add layers of clothing."
    new "Now, as luck would have it, Triberg was in for an especially harsh weather that year. Not too harsh, understand, as Triberg has always had moderate climate, but cold enough that for the first time many people were looking to add layers of clothing.\n而碰巧的是，那年 Triberg 将迎来格外严寒的天气。别误会，也不算太严酷，毕竟 Triberg 气候一向温和，但冷得足以让许多人头一次想着多添几层衣服。"

    old "It seemed like an opportunity. I bought up furs from around GrandTree, most of them costing me two or three gold pieces for a dozen, and transported them down to Triberg, where they sold for eight to ten gold pieces for a dozen."
    new "It seemed like an opportunity. I bought up furs from around GrandTree, most of them costing me two or three gold pieces for a dozen, and transported them down to Triberg, where they sold for eight to ten gold pieces for a dozen.\n这看起来是个机会。我收购了 GrandTree 一带的毛皮，多数进价是一打两三枚金币，再把它们运到 Triberg，在那里一打能卖八到十枚金币。"

    old "Now, if you buy something for two gold pieces, and sell it for ten gold pieces, where did the eight gold pieces of profit come from? They're a measure of the wealth you created."
    new "Now, if you buy something for two gold pieces, and sell it for ten gold pieces, where did the eight gold pieces of profit come from? They're a measure of the wealth you created.\n那么，如果你用两枚金币买进某样东西，再以十枚金币卖出，那八枚金币的利润从何而来？它们正是你所创造的财富的度量。"

    old "Make no mistake: real value was created there. Remember, an object's value is measured by how much people want. In a hot weather climate, a fur is less valuable than it is in a cold weather climate. So you can add to the value of a fur simply by changing its location. That's why so many merchants are involved in the transportation of goods."
    new "Make no mistake: real value was created there. Remember, an object's value is measured by how much people want. In a hot weather climate, a fur is less valuable than it is in a cold weather climate. So you can add to the value of a fur simply by changing its location. That's why so many merchants are involved in the transportation of goods.\n别搞错了：那里确实创造了真正的价值。记住，一件物品的价值，由人们对它的渴求程度来衡量。在炎热的气候里，毛皮的价值不如在寒冷气候里高。所以，你只需改变毛皮的位置，就能提升它的价值。这就是为什么那么多商人都投身于货物运输。"

    old "Sometimes, simply knowing what the weather is going to be like several months from now can help me make a wise business decision, which is why I'm so interested in keeping in contact with such a large variety of friends. It helps me remain informed on a myriad of topics. That's exactly how I managed to make so much transporting furs to Triberg during their harsh winter."
    new "Sometimes, simply knowing what the weather is going to be like several months from now can help me make a wise business decision, which is why I'm so interested in keeping in contact with such a large variety of friends. It helps me remain informed on a myriad of topics. That's exactly how I managed to make so much transporting furs to Triberg during their harsh winter.\n有时候，仅仅知道几个月后天气会怎样，就能帮我做出明智的商业决策。这正是我热衷于跟形形色色的朋友保持联系的原因——这让我能对五花八门的话题了如指掌。我正是靠这个，才在他们那个严冬把毛皮运到 Triberg，赚了那么多。"

    old "That's clever. You saw a need, and you found a way to meet it."
    new "That's clever. You saw a need, and you found a way to meet it.\n真聪明。你看到了需求，又想出了满足它的办法。"

    old "I'm glad you think so. I'll admit that luck had a little to do with it, but luck is where preparation intersects with opportunity."
    new "I'm glad you think so. I'll admit that luck had a little to do with it, but luck is where preparation intersects with opportunity.\n很高兴你这么想。我承认其中有点运气的成分，但所谓运气，不过是准备与机遇的交汇。"

    old "How did you manage to sell the furs at an inflated price? It seems like you were charging a significant markup."
    new "How did you manage to sell the furs at an inflated price? It seems like you were charging a significant markup.\n你是怎么把毛皮卖出虚高价格的？你似乎加了相当高的价。"

    old "That's opportunistic. People were in a state of need, and you took advantage of their dire situation."
    new "That's opportunistic. People were in a state of need, and you took advantage of their dire situation.\n那是投机取巧。人们正陷于困顿，你却利用了他们的窘境。"

    old "Tell me, [protag]. Is it opportunistic for a baker to target the hungry when hawking his goods? Is it opportunistic for a blacksmith to ramp up his production of swords in times of war?"
    new "Tell me, [protag]. Is it opportunistic for a baker to target the hungry when hawking his goods? Is it opportunistic for a blacksmith to ramp up his production of swords in times of war?\n告诉我，[protag]。面包师吆喝叫卖时，把饿肚子的人当作主顾，算投机吗？铁匠在战时加紧打造刀剑，算投机吗？"

    old "You sold goods to them at an inflated price."
    new "You sold goods to them at an inflated price.\n你以虚高的价格把货卖给了他们。"

    old "I charged what the market would bear. I sold the furs for what they were worth. If the people of Triberg hadn't valued them at the price I was charging, they wouldn't have bought them."
    new "I charged what the market would bear. I sold the furs for what they were worth. If the people of Triberg hadn't valued them at the price I was charging, they wouldn't have bought them.\n我开的价是市场能承受的价。我按毛皮应有的价值出售。如果 Triberg 的人觉得我开的价不值那些毛皮，他们就不会买。"

    old "It's not as if those people had no gold to spend. For many of them, finding the extra gold to buy fur clothing was as simple as forgoing a nice meal."
    new "It's not as if those people had no gold to spend. For many of them, finding the extra gold to buy fur clothing was as simple as forgoing a nice meal.\n那些人又不是没有金币可花。对他们许多人来说，凑出买毛皮衣物的额外金币，简单得就像省下一顿好饭。"

    old "They decided that having warm clothing to wear was more important than having delicious food, so for a few weeks of the winter they ate bread instead of meat and drank water instead of ale, and when all was said and done, they enjoyed the winter in much more warmth than they might have otherwise."
    new "They decided that having warm clothing to wear was more important than having delicious food, so for a few weeks of the winter they ate bread instead of meat and drank water instead of ale, and when all was said and done, they enjoyed the winter in much more warmth than they might have otherwise.\n他们认定，有暖和的衣服穿比吃美味佳肴更重要，于是在那年冬天的几周里，他们吃面包代替肉、喝水代替麦酒。等一切尘埃落定，他们比原本可能的情况暖和得多地度过了冬天。"

    old "Many people even paid for their furs simply by burning less wood or coal that winter. In fact, some of them found that bundling up in warmer clothing actually saved them money in the long run."
    new "Many people even paid for their furs simply by burning less wood or coal that winter. In fact, some of them found that bundling up in warmer clothing actually saved them money in the long run.\n许多人甚至只靠那个冬天少烧些木柴或煤炭，就付清了毛皮钱。事实上，有些人发现，裹上更暖和的衣服从长远看反而省了钱。"

    old "Still others decided not to purchase my furs at all, and they turned instead to wool garments, or they burned more wood and coal for warmth, or maybe they even learned to endure the cold for a short while."
    new "Still others decided not to purchase my furs at all, and they turned instead to wool garments, or they burned more wood and coal for warmth, or maybe they even learned to endure the cold for a short while.\n还有些人干脆决定不买我的毛皮，转而改穿羊毛衣裳，或者多烧木柴和煤炭取暖，甚至有人学会了短期内忍受寒冷。"

    old "My point is, at no point did I compel the people of Triberg to purchase furs from me. It was a decision that they made of their free will. And for many of them, the decision was one that left them happy."
    new "My point is, at no point did I compel the people of Triberg to purchase furs from me. It was a decision that they made of their free will. And for many of them, the decision was one that left them happy.\n我的意思是，我从未在任何时刻强迫 Triberg 的人向我购买毛皮。那是他们凭自由意志做出的决定。对他们许多人来说，这个决定让他们心满意足。"

    old "In fact, one city official publicly thanked me for coming through. You see, the city realized that their citizens would have a need for warmer clothes in the winter months, and they wanted to take action, but you know how city councils are."
    new "In fact, one city official publicly thanked me for coming through. You see, the city realized that their citizens would have a need for warmer clothes in the winter months, and they wanted to take action, but you know how city councils are.\n事实上，有位市政官员公开感谢我帮了大忙。你看，城里意识到市民在冬季会需要更暖和的衣物，也想采取行动，但你知道市政议会是什么德性。"

    old "They're bureaucratic and slow-moving. By the time they had authorized the action, the chill had already begun to set in. It would have taken months for them to actually place and fill an order from a nearby city. Luckily, I had anticipated their needs, and I was able to be there in time for the winter."
    new "They're bureaucratic and slow-moving. By the time they had authorized the action, the chill had already begun to set in. It would have taken months for them to actually place and fill an order from a nearby city. Luckily, I had anticipated their needs, and I was able to be there in time for the winter.\n他们官僚又拖沓。等他们批准行动时，寒意已经开始袭来了。真要向邻近城市下单并到货，得花上好几个月。幸运的是，我早就预见到了他们的需求，得以赶在冬天及时赶到。"

    old "And you reaped the profits."
    new "And you reaped the profits.\n于是你坐收了利润。"

    old "Yes, I am a merchant, and like any practitioner of any profession, I expect to be rewarded when I do my job well. In that case, my ability to read the market, make a prediction, and take decisive action turned out to be spot on."
    new "Yes, I am a merchant, and like any practitioner of any profession, I expect to be rewarded when I do my job well. In that case, my ability to read the market, make a prediction, and take decisive action turned out to be spot on.\n没错，我是个商人，和任何行业的从业者一样，把本职工作做好时，我理应得到回报。在那件事上，我解读市场、做出预判、果断出手的能力，最终被证明分毫不差。"

    old "Information is what allows me to make those 'big plays.' I'm always on the lookout for influencers, but oftentimes, someone can be an asset to my business simply by helping to keep me well-informed. You strike me as the type of person who knows a lot about what's going on in the world."
    new "Information is what allows me to make those 'big plays.' I'm always on the lookout for influencers, but oftentimes, someone can be an asset to my business simply by helping to keep me well-informed. You strike me as the type of person who knows a lot about what's going on in the world.\n让我做出那些‘大动作’的，正是情报。我总是在物色有影响力的人，但很多时候，一个人只需帮我保持消息灵通，就能成为我生意上的资产。在我看来，你就是那种对世上风吹草动都了如指掌的人。"

    old "That being said, I don't expect you to divulge all of your secrets to me, especially when I'm not prepared at the moment to offer much of anything in return. But I'm glad you were willing to take the time to meet with me, and I hope to see you again in the future."
    new "That being said, I don't expect you to divulge all of your secrets to me, especially when I'm not prepared at the moment to offer much of anything in return. But I'm glad you were willing to take the time to meet with me, and I hope to see you again in the future.\n话虽如此，我并不指望你把所有秘密都对我倾囊相告，尤其是我此刻还拿不出什么像样的回报。但我很高兴你愿意抽出时间见我，希望日后还能再会。"

    old "I find Lady Geraldine in her mansion's gardens."
    new "I find Lady Geraldine in her mansion's gardens.\n我在她宅邸的花园里找到了 Geraldine 夫人。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. What brings you to me this fine day?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. What brings you to me this fine day?\n啊，[protag]。今天是什么风把你吹到我这儿来了？"

    old "I'm just here to make conversation."
    new "I'm just here to make conversation.\n我只是来聊聊的。"

    old "Conversation? That's a word that can mean many things. Conversations are funny things. You can say so much without saying anything directly."
    new "Conversation? That's a word that can mean many things. Conversations are funny things. You can say so much without saying anything directly.\n聊聊？这个词可以有很多含义。交谈是件有趣的事。你可以不直接挑明，却传递出许多意思。"

    old "Suppose I have a shipment that is being tied up because the city has issued an embargo on foreign imports. I need to get those furs into Lothark, and someone in Grimoire's council is preventing me from doing it, so I pay them a visit."
    new "Suppose I have a shipment that is being tied up because the city has issued an embargo on foreign imports. I need to get those furs into Lothark, and someone in Grimoire's council is preventing me from doing it, so I pay them a visit.\n假设我有一批货被扣住了，因为城里对外国进口下了禁令。我需要把那些毛皮运进 Lothark，而 Grimoire 议会里有人从中作梗，于是我上门拜访了他们。"

    old "A secret meeting?"
    new "A secret meeting?\n一次秘密会面？"

    old "No, not a secret meeting. A meeting in public. The kind that people can observe and even overhear from a distance and not find me guilty of any kind of bribery in the eyes of the law."
    new "No, not a secret meeting. A meeting in public. The kind that people can observe and even overhear from a distance and not find me guilty of any kind of bribery in the eyes of the law.\n不，不是秘密会面。是公开会面。那种人们能从远处看到、甚至听到，却不会在法律眼中认定我犯下任何贿赂之罪的会面。"

    old "If you're not going to bribe the official, then how do you persuade them to your cause?"
    new "If you're not going to bribe the official, then how do you persuade them to your cause?\n如果你不打算贿赂那位官员，那要怎么说服他站到你这边？"

    old "Oh, my sweet child. I said that I wouldn't be found guilty of bribery in the eyes of the law. That's quite a bit different from abstaining from bribery entirely."
    new "Oh, my sweet child. I said that I wouldn't be found guilty of bribery in the eyes of the law. That's quite a bit different from abstaining from bribery entirely.\n哦，我亲爱的孩子。我说的是我不会在法律眼中被判贿赂之罪。这和彻底不做贿赂，可大不一样。"

    old "So you bribe them without actually bribing them."
    new "So you bribe them without actually bribing them.\n所以你是贿赂了他们，却又没有真正贿赂。"

    old "It's quite easy. Saying things without actually saying things is how I do business when it comes to dealing with politicians."
    new "It's quite easy. Saying things without actually saying things is how I do business when it comes to dealing with politicians.\n这很简单。把话说出口，却又没有真正说出口——这就是我跟政客打交道时的做派。"

    old "Give me an example."
    new "Give me an example.\n给我举个例子。"

    old "'Oh, hello there, councilman. I hear your daughter has a wedding coming up. A girl as beautiful as your daughter deserves to be clad in the finest of linen dresses on her wedding day, don't you think? Wouldn't it be wonderful if she could find a tailor who could offer her fine linens for a tiny fraction of their retail price?"
    new "'Oh, hello there, councilman. I hear your daughter has a wedding coming up. A girl as beautiful as your daughter deserves to be clad in the finest of linen dresses on her wedding day, don't you think? Wouldn't it be wonderful if she could find a tailor who could offer her fine linens for a tiny fraction of their retail price?\n‘哦，你好啊，议员先生。我听说令嫒婚期将近。像令嫒这般美丽的姑娘，婚礼当天理应穿上最上等的亚麻礼服，你说是不是？要是她能找到一位裁缝，只用零售价的一个零头就为她备好上等亚麻料子，那该多好啊？’"

    old "I know men in your position will often spend as much as two month's salary on a wedding dress for their daughter, so to be able to find one at a significant discount...what a fortunate thing that would be indeed. Well, goodbye, councilman. Have a pleasant day.'"
    new "I know men in your position will often spend as much as two month's salary on a wedding dress for their daughter, so to be able to find one at a significant discount...what a fortunate thing that would be indeed. Well, goodbye, councilman. Have a pleasant day.'\n我知道，像您这样身份的人，常常会为女儿的婚纱花掉足足两个月的薪水。所以要是能以大幅折扣买到一件……那可真是天大的幸事。好了，再会，议员先生。祝您愉快。’"

    old "So you don't even put an offer on the table."
    new "So you don't even put an offer on the table.\n所以你甚至都不把条件摆到台面上。"

    old "No, but I make it clear what I have to offer."
    new "No, but I make it clear what I have to offer.\n没错，但我把‘我能提供什么’说得明明白白。"

    old "I must have missed the part where you tell him what he gives you in exchange."
    new "I must have missed the part where you tell him what he gives you in exchange.\n我一定是漏掉了你告诉他‘他要拿什么来交换’的那部分。"

    old "I don't need to tell him, [protag]. Any councilman worth bribing will already know what I want when I sit down to talk with him. Again, this is how I'm able to communicate so much while saying very little. The fact that these words are coming from my lips specifically is part of the message."
    new "I don't need to tell him, [protag]. Any councilman worth bribing will already know what I want when I sit down to talk with him. Again, this is how I'm able to communicate so much while saying very little. The fact that these words are coming from my lips specifically is part of the message.\n我不必告诉他，[protag]。任何值得我去贿赂的议员，在我坐下来同他交谈时，就已经明白我想要什么了。再说一遍，这正是我能用寥寥数语传递出许多意思的诀窍。这些话偏偏出自我的口中，这本身就是信息的一部分。"

    old "Why the need for all of this innuendo? You know that you're offering him a bribe, and he knows that you're offering him a bribe, and you know that he knows and he knows that you know, so the idea of plausible deniablility doesn't really enter into it. Just meet in private and say what you really mean."
    new "Why the need for all of this innuendo? You know that you're offering him a bribe, and he knows that you're offering him a bribe, and you know that he knows and he knows that you know, so the idea of plausible deniablility doesn't really enter into it. Just meet in private and say what you really mean.\n何必搞这些弯弯绕绕？你知道自己在向他行贿，他也知道你在向他行贿，你知道他知道、他也知道你知道，所以什么‘可推诿否认’根本无从谈起。私下见面，直说你的真实意图不就行了。"

    old "Private meetings look suspicious. People might begin to suspect me and the hypothetical councilman of collusion if we disappeared into a room together to discuss things in private. In the commercial district of a place like Grimoire or Lothark, secret meetings aren't quite so secret. Why, I'm sure that your visit to me today won't remain a secret."
    new "Private meetings look suspicious. People might begin to suspect me and the hypothetical councilman of collusion if we disappeared into a room together to discuss things in private. In the commercial district of a place like Grimoire or Lothark, secret meetings aren't quite so secret. Why, I'm sure that your visit to me today won't remain a secret.\n私下会面显得可疑。要是我和那位假想中的议员一起消失在某间屋子里私下议事，人们恐怕会开始怀疑我俩勾结。在 Grimoire 或 Lothark 这类地方的商业区，秘密会面可没那么秘密。喏，我敢肯定，你今天来拜访我这件事也保不住密。"

    old "I'm a target for spies?"
    new "I'm a target for spies?\n我成了间谍的目标？"

    old "You're not the target. I am."
    new "You're not the target. I am.\n你不是目标。我才是。"

    old "And spies? No, my dear. Not spies. You might call them 'commercial informants.' These aren't spies sent by a foreign government to uncover a nation's secrets. They're the eyes and ears of rival merchants, trying to stay one step ahead of the competition."
    new "And spies? No, my dear. Not spies. You might call them 'commercial informants.' These aren't spies sent by a foreign government to uncover a nation's secrets. They're the eyes and ears of rival merchants, trying to stay one step ahead of the competition.\n间谍？不，亲爱的。不是间谍。你或许可以叫他们‘商业线人’。他们不是外国政府派来刺探国家机密的间谍，而是对手商人的耳目，一心要在竞争中抢占先机。"

    old "I'm not above using them myself. How do you think it is that the first time you came to Lothark, I was the first person who managed to get your attention?"
    new "I'm not above using them myself. How do you think it is that the first time you came to Lothark, I was the first person who managed to get your attention?\n我自己也不排斥使唤他们。你想想，你头一回来 Lothark 时，怎么偏偏是我第一个引起了你的注意？"

    old "It certainly wasn't coincidence that led you to me. I know what happens in this city. So do my rivals."
    new "It certainly wasn't coincidence that led you to me. I know what happens in this city. So do my rivals.\n把你引到我面前的，绝不是巧合。这座城市里发生什么，我一清二楚。我的对手们也一样。"

    old "Why are your rivals spying on you?"
    new "Why are your rivals spying on you?\n你的对手们为什么要监视你？"

    old "Again with that word, 'spying.' 'Spy' is a word with a very specific meaning. It means someone in the employ of the government sent out to obtain information from foreign countries, usually the kind of people who are concerned with gathering information about a nation's military."
    new "Again with that word, 'spying.' 'Spy' is a word with a very specific meaning. It means someone in the employ of the government sent out to obtain information from foreign countries, usually the kind of people who are concerned with gathering information about a nation's military.\n你又来了，‘监视’。‘间谍’是个含义非常明确的词。它指的是受政府雇用、被派往外国搜集情报的人，通常是一心收集别国军事情报的那种人。"

    old "I know of only one person in this city that answers to that description, and [heshe] is standing right in front of me."
    new "I know of only one person in this city that answers to that description, and [heshe] is standing right in front of me.\n这座城市里符合这一描述的，我只知道有一个人，而 [heshe] 此刻就站在我面前。"

    old "You think I'm a spy?"
    new "You think I'm a spy?\n你以为我是间谍？"

    old "You're employed by the government of Grimoire, and you were sent out to gather information, mostly of military significance, from the lands outside of the human empire. That's what you were doing in that castle out in the plains, wasn't it? Gathering information that the Grimoire military is now acting on? That's what spying is, my dear."
    new "You're employed by the government of Grimoire, and you were sent out to gather information, mostly of military significance, from the lands outside of the human empire. That's what you were doing in that castle out in the plains, wasn't it? Gathering information that the Grimoire military is now acting on? That's what spying is, my dear.\n你受雇于 Grimoire 政府，被派到人类帝国之外的领土上搜集情报，大多还是具有军事意义的情报。你在平原上那座城堡里干的，不就是这个吗？搜集 Grimoire 军队如今正在据此行动的情报？亲爱的，这就是间谍活动。"

    old "You said it's likely that someone is watching our meeting."
    new "You said it's likely that someone is watching our meeting.\n你说很可能有人在盯着我们的会面。"

    old "Not watching our meeting, per se, but there is likely someone watching my door at all hours of the day. Not in any nefarious way, you realize. Most of these informants are actually rather normal people."
    new "Not watching our meeting, per se, but there is likely someone watching my door at all hours of the day. Not in any nefarious way, you realize. Most of these informants are actually rather normal people.\n倒不是盯着我们的会面本身，而是很可能一天到晚都有人在盯着我家门口。你要明白，这并非什么见不得光的勾当。这些线人大多其实都是相当普通的人。"

    old "Perhaps a fish vendor who travels around town, and takes mental notes on the things he observes as he peddles his ware. Or it could simply be a child, looking for a way to spend his day and make some coin by auctioning his information off to the highest bidder."
    new "Perhaps a fish vendor who travels around town, and takes mental notes on the things he observes as he peddles his ware. Or it could simply be a child, looking for a way to spend his day and make some coin by auctioning his information off to the highest bidder.\n也许是某个走街串巷的鱼贩，一边吆喝卖货，一边把看到的事情默默记在心里。又或者只是个孩子，想打发一天的光景，把自己的消息卖给开价最高的人，好赚几个铜板。"

    old "The streets weren't empty when you came to my manor, and so someone probably knows that you are here, and has probably sold that information to one of my rivals. That isn't unusual at all, [protag]. That's simply how business is done here amongst the merchants of Lothark."
    new "The streets weren't empty when you came to my manor, and so someone probably knows that you are here, and has probably sold that information to one of my rivals. That isn't unusual at all, [protag]. That's simply how business is done here amongst the merchants of Lothark.\n你来我府邸时，街上并非空无一人，所以多半有人知道你来了，而且很可能已把那消息卖给了我的某个对手。这一点都不稀奇，[protag]。在 Lothark 的商人圈子里，生意就是这么做的。"

    old "Why are your rivals watching you? Are they trying to accuse you of some kind of wrongdoing?"
    new "Why are your rivals watching you? Are they trying to accuse you of some kind of wrongdoing?\n你的对手们为什么盯着你？他们是想指控你干了什么坏事吗？"

    old "No, no, no, my dear. You've got it all wrong. People don't spy on their rivals to expose them. Knowledge is power, you see, and that power becomes diluted the more that knowledge is spread. If one of my business rivals did become aware of shady dealings on my part, they wouldn't report me to the government. They'd try to exploit the situation for their own profit."
    new "No, no, no, my dear. You've got it all wrong. People don't spy on their rivals to expose them. Knowledge is power, you see, and that power becomes diluted the more that knowledge is spread. If one of my business rivals did become aware of shady dealings on my part, they wouldn't report me to the government. They'd try to exploit the situation for their own profit.\n不不不，亲爱的。你完全搞错了。人们监视对手，不是为了揭发他们。你看，知识就是力量，而知识传播得越广，那份力量就越被稀释。就算我的某个商业对手真察觉到我有见不得人的勾当，他们也不会向政府举报我，反而会想方设法利用这局面为自己牟利。"

    old "For example, if in a single week I have separate meetings with a textiles merchant, a well-known tailor, and a carpenter who specializes in loom construction, my rivals could intuit that I was planning something involving the manufacture and sale of clothing."
    new "For example, if in a single week I have separate meetings with a textiles merchant, a well-known tailor, and a carpenter who specializes in loom construction, my rivals could intuit that I was planning something involving the manufacture and sale of clothing.\n比方说，如果我在一周之内分别会见了纺织品商人、知名裁缝，以及一位专造织布机的木匠，我的对手们就能推断出，我在筹划某桩与服装产销有关的事情。"

    old "So why is it that you're so willing to meet with me? If your rivals saw me entering the building, then I'm giving them information just by being here."
    new "So why is it that you're so willing to meet with me? If your rivals saw me entering the building, then I'm giving them information just by being here.\n那你为什么还这么乐意与我见面？如果你的对手看到我走进这栋楼，那我光是待在这里，就等于给他们递了消息。"

    old "Oh, I'm perfectly fine with that. And I want them to know. You see, people know who you are, [protag]. They know that you're the council's emissary. So every time you come to visit me, it has the effect of making me look like a very important person."
    new "Oh, I'm perfectly fine with that. And I want them to know. You see, people know who you are, [protag]. They know that you're the council's emissary. So every time you come to visit me, it has the effect of making me look like a very important person.\n哦，我完全不在乎，而且我还巴不得他们知道。你看，人们知道你是谁，[protag]。他们知道你是议会的使者。所以你每次登门拜访，都会让我显得像个举足轻重的大人物。"

    old "You were already plenty important before I started visiting you."
    new "You were already plenty important before I started visiting you.\n在我开始拜访你之前，你早就够有分量了。"

    old "But importance is such a transitory thing, [protag]. If someone who is a very important person does nothing for an entire year, their importance doesn't stay stagnant. No, they decline in importance."
    new "But importance is such a transitory thing, [protag]. If someone who is a very important person does nothing for an entire year, their importance doesn't stay stagnant. No, they decline in importance.\n但所谓分量，是如此转瞬即逝的东西，[protag]。要是一个举足轻重的人整整一年无所作为，他的分量不会原地踏步。不，会渐渐消减。"

    old "Importance is a resource that you need to cultivate, and saying that I have no need to make myself more important because I'm already an important person is just as ludicrous as telling a man that he has no need to gather food because he has just eaten."
    new "Importance is a resource that you need to cultivate, and saying that I have no need to make myself more important because I'm already an important person is just as ludicrous as telling a man that he has no need to gather food because he has just eaten.\n分量是一种需要用心经营的资源。说什么‘我已经是重要人物，没必要再抬高自己’，就跟告诉一个人‘你刚吃过饭，不用再囤粮食’一样荒唐。"

    old "What exactly do you hope to gain from our visits?"
    new "What exactly do you hope to gain from our visits?\n你究竟希望从我们的会面中得到什么？"

    old "Well, as I've told you, my intentions are partially mercenary. I'm here because your visits make me seem more important. But quite frankly, my time is too valuable to spend just in the pursuit of prestige. No, the reason that I'm willing to entertain you rather than some other potentially noteworthy guests is that I enjoy your company, [protag]."
    new "Well, as I've told you, my intentions are partially mercenary. I'm here because your visits make me seem more important. But quite frankly, my time is too valuable to spend just in the pursuit of prestige. No, the reason that I'm willing to entertain you rather than some other potentially noteworthy guests is that I enjoy your company, [protag].\n这个嘛，正如我对你说过的，我的意图里有一部分是功利的。我来见你，是因为你的拜访让我显得更有分量。但坦白说，我的时间太宝贵，不该只花在沽名钓誉上。不，我之所以愿意招待你，而不是其他那些可能同样值得一见的客人，是因为我享受你的陪伴，[protag]。"

    old "I'm not sure what exactly I've done to win your favor. It seems that our 'meetings' mostly consist of you talking about yourself."
    new "I'm not sure what exactly I've done to win your favor. It seems that our 'meetings' mostly consist of you talking about yourself.\n我不确定自己究竟做了什么，才赢得你的青睐。我们的‘会面’似乎大多是你在谈论你自己。"

    old "The fiber of your person is not measured in how much you talk, [protag]. In fact, if you spend much time in Grimoire council meetings, I think you'll often find that the most important ones in the room are the ones whose speech is most seldom."
    new "The fiber of your person is not measured in how much you talk, [protag]. In fact, if you spend much time in Grimoire council meetings, I think you'll often find that the most important ones in the room are the ones whose speech is most seldom.\n一个人的品格，不是以他话多话少来衡量的，[protag]。事实上，如果你常在 Grimoire 议会的会议上待着，我想你会经常发现，屋里最举足轻重的，往往是那些最少开口的人。"

    old "You're right when you say that most of the time we spend together consists of me talking about my own affairs and you reacting to them. But your reactions interest me."
    new "You're right when you say that most of the time we spend together consists of me talking about my own affairs and you reacting to them. But your reactions interest me.\n你说得对，我们共处的大多数时间，都是我在谈论自己的事，而你对此做出回应。但你的回应让我很感兴趣。"

    old "You're not an interesting person because of what you say when you're around me. You're interesting because of who you are. As far as I understand, before this whole business with the vampires and the N'Mar castle began, you were a relative nobody."
    new "You're not an interesting person because of what you say when you're around me. You're interesting because of who you are. As far as I understand, before this whole business with the vampires and the N'Mar castle began, you were a relative nobody.\n你之所以有趣，不是因为在我身边时说了什么，而是因为你本身。据我所知，在 Vampires 和 N'Mar 城堡这整件事开始之前，你只是个无足轻重的小人物。"

    old "And almost overnight, it seems like you've been elevated to a very important role in all of this. Not many people can claim to represent the interests of Grimoire's council."
    new "And almost overnight, it seems like you've been elevated to a very important role in all of this. Not many people can claim to represent the interests of Grimoire's council.\n而几乎是一夜之间，你似乎就被擢升到了这一切当中举足轻重的位置。没有多少人能声称自己代表 Grimoire 议会的利益。"

    old "I've asked myself, what is it that makes you so special? I suspect that you yourself might not know the answer to this question, and so I think that the best thing for me to do might be to simply sit back and observe you. I spout various platitudes, and depending on how you react, or fail to react, I gain a bit of insight into who you are."
    new "I've asked myself, what is it that makes you so special? I suspect that you yourself might not know the answer to this question, and so I think that the best thing for me to do might be to simply sit back and observe you. I spout various platitudes, and depending on how you react, or fail to react, I gain a bit of insight into who you are.\n我问过自己，究竟是什么让你如此特别？我猜你自己或许也不知道这个问题的答案。所以我想，我最好就坐在一旁观察你。我抛出各种陈词滥调，再根据你作何反应——或者毫无反应——来窥见你的为人一二。"

    old "And why do I care? Mostly, I'm just curious. Because while it's often tempting to measure my success in terms of wealth and influence, the thing that I value most is understanding and insight."
    new "And why do I care? Mostly, I'm just curious. Because while it's often tempting to measure my success in terms of wealth and influence, the thing that I value most is understanding and insight.\n我为什么要在意呢？大多只是出于好奇。因为虽然用财富和影响力来衡量我的成就是件诱人的事，但我最看重的，还是理解和洞见。"

    old "The most satisfying visits and meetings I have are not the ones that result in a lucrative business deal, but the ones that result in me coming to new conclusions and discovering new ideas."
    new "The most satisfying visits and meetings I have are not the ones that result in a lucrative business deal, but the ones that result in me coming to new conclusions and discovering new ideas.\n我最满意的拜访与会面，不是那些带来丰厚生意交易的，而是那些让我得出新结论、发现新想法的。"

    old "Of course, you may one day prove useful to me. That, I am also banking on, because my experience has taught me that fascinating people often tend to be at the epicenter of lucrative business opportunities. But the fascination itself is more worth the time I spend talking to you."
    new "Of course, you may one day prove useful to me. That, I am also banking on, because my experience has taught me that fascinating people often tend to be at the epicenter of lucrative business opportunities. But the fascination itself is more worth the time I spend talking to you.\n当然，有朝一日你或许会对我有用。这一点我也押了注，因为经验告诉我，引人入胜的人往往处在丰厚商机的中心。不过，那份引人入胜本身，就比我花在与你交谈上的时间更值得。"

    old "What kind of person are you, [protag]? How do you see yourself?"
    new "What kind of person are you, [protag]? How do you see yourself?\n你是什么样的人，[protag]？你如何看待自己？"

    old "I'm an ordinary person."
    new "I'm an ordinary person.\n我是个普通人。"

    old "And yet you've accomplished extraordinary things."
    new "And yet you've accomplished extraordinary things.\n可你却成就了非凡之事。"

    old "I didn't invade N'Mar all by myself. Perhaps I just have a knack for surrounding myself with extraordinary people."
    new "I didn't invade N'Mar all by myself. Perhaps I just have a knack for surrounding myself with extraordinary people.\n我并不是单枪匹马攻进 N'Mar 的。也许我只是天生擅长让自己身边聚满非凡之人。"

    old "But isn't that in itself an exceptional talent? Someone with a knack for gathering the talented and putting them to work solving difficult tasks, I think there's a name for that skillset. I think it's called 'leadership.'"
    new "But isn't that in itself an exceptional talent? Someone with a knack for gathering the talented and putting them to work solving difficult tasks, I think there's a name for that skillset. I think it's called 'leadership.'\n但那本身难道不就是一种出众的才华吗？有本事把人才聚拢起来，再派他们去攻克难题——我想这种能力有个名字。我想它叫‘领导力’。"

    old "You call it skill, but it might just as easily by luck. It's not inconceivable that someone simply wandering around at random might happen to surround themselves with a collection of talented people."
    new "You call it skill, but it might just as easily by luck. It's not inconceivable that someone simply wandering around at random might happen to surround themselves with a collection of talented people.\n你说那是本领，但也完全可能是运气。一个人随便东游西荡，碰巧身边聚起一群有才之士，这也不是不可想象。"

    old "Well, if it's luck and not skill that's brought you to where you are today, then you must be the luckiest [manwoman] alive. And maybe if I keep spending time with you, some of that good luck will rub off on me."
    new "Well, if it's luck and not skill that's brought you to where you are today, then you must be the luckiest [manwoman] alive. And maybe if I keep spending time with you, some of that good luck will rub off on me.\n那么，如果把你带到今天这个位置的，是运气而非本领，那你一定是天底下最幸运的 [manwoman] 了。也许我继续跟你待在一起，那些好运也能沾到我身上一点。"

    old "I don't think it works like that. Good luck isn't contagious."
    new "I don't think it works like that. Good luck isn't contagious.\n我觉得不是那么回事。好运可不会传染。"

    old "Isn't it? Don't forget, the copious talented people that you've surrounded yourself with, they've shared in your victories. So in that sense, your 'good luck' has been contagious."
    new "Isn't it? Don't forget, the copious talented people that you've surrounded yourself with, they've shared in your victories. So in that sense, your 'good luck' has been contagious.\n不会吗？别忘了，你身边那许多有才之士，都分享过你的胜利。所以从那个意义上说，你的‘好运’确实传染了。"

    old "I wouldn't be so quick to ascribe to random chance what seems to be a very consistent pattern of exceptional achievement. False humility isn't a virtue, [protag]."
    new "I wouldn't be so quick to ascribe to random chance what seems to be a very consistent pattern of exceptional achievement. False humility isn't a virtue, [protag].\n我可不急着把一连串始终如一的非凡成就归因于随机偶然。虚假的谦逊不是美德，[protag]。"

    old "What if it's not false humility?"
    new "What if it's not false humility?\n如果那不是虚假的谦逊呢？"

    old "Then it means you're delusional. And I mean that in the most affectionate way possible."
    new "Then it means you're delusional. And I mean that in the most affectionate way possible.\n那就说明你在妄想。而且我是用最亲切的方式说这话的。"

    old "I guess I'll have to take it as a compliment, then. But it's not often I hear the word 'delusional' used as a term of endearment or praise."
    new "I guess I'll have to take it as a compliment, then. But it's not often I hear the word 'delusional' used as a term of endearment or praise.\n那我想我只好把它当作夸奖了。不过，我可不常听到‘妄想’这个词被拿来当作爱称或赞美。"

    old "I'm an extraordinary person."
    new "I'm an extraordinary person.\n我是个非凡的人。"

    old "Geraldine claps her hands together in delight."
    new "Geraldine claps her hands together in delight.\nGeraldine 夫人欣喜地拍起手来。"

    old "See, you recognize your own talent. What is it that causes you to describe yourself as extraordinary?"
    new "See, you recognize your own talent. What is it that causes you to describe yourself as extraordinary?\n瞧，你认得自己的才华。是什么让你把自己形容为非凡？"

    old "It's because of who I am as a person."
    new "It's because of who I am as a person.\n因为我的为人本身。"

    old "Interesting. So you say that it's in your blood. You've always been this way. Even years ago, before circumstance thrust you into the limelight."
    new "Interesting. So you say that it's in your blood. You've always been this way. Even years ago, before circumstance thrust you into the limelight.\n有意思。所以你说这是骨子里的。你一向如此。甚至在多年前，在境遇把你推上聚光灯之前，也是如此。"

    old "Yes, I think that great people are always great. It's not as if circumstance can take a person with no potential and mold them into a great achiever."
    new "Yes, I think that great people are always great. It's not as if circumstance can take a person with no potential and mold them into a great achiever.\n是的，我认为伟大的人始终伟大。境遇可没法把一个毫无潜力的人塑造成伟大的成就者。"

    old "Any great painter had the gift of artistry in them even before the moment when they first picked up a paintbrush. Every great general had some kind of spark in them, even when they were just a lowly private. It can take time, sometimes years or even a lifetime, but eventually those people will realize their potential."
    new "Any great painter had the gift of artistry in them even before the moment when they first picked up a paintbrush. Every great general had some kind of spark in them, even when they were just a lowly private. It can take time, sometimes years or even a lifetime, but eventually those people will realize their potential.\n任何伟大的画家，早在第一次拿起画笔之前，体内就藏着艺术天赋。每位伟大的将领，哪怕还只是个低微的士兵时，体内也有某种火花。这需要时间，有时是数年，甚至是一辈子，但那些人最终都会兑现自己的潜能。"

    old "It always seems like great achievers come out of extraordinary circumstances. But I don't think that the cirumstances make great people. It simply reveals them."
    new "It always seems like great achievers come out of extraordinary circumstances. But I don't think that the cirumstances make great people. It simply reveals them.\n伟大的成就者似乎总是出自非凡的境遇。但我不认为境遇造就了伟人。境遇只是把他们显露出来。"

    old "So you believe that you were always a diamond in the rough, just waiting to be discovered."
    new "So you believe that you were always a diamond in the rough, just waiting to be discovered.\n所以你认为自己一直是块未经雕琢的璞玉，只等着被人发现。"

    old "I'm not sure if I'd compare myself to a diamond. But I agree the sentiment."
    new "I'm not sure if I'd compare myself to a diamond. But I agree the sentiment.\n我不确定自己是否会把自己比作钻石。但我认同那份心意。"

    old "It's because of the things I've accomplished."
    new "It's because of the things I've accomplished.\n是因为我成就的那些事。"

    old "A year ago, I was on a fundamental level very much the same person that I am today, at my core. I've had new experiences since then, and changed some of my ideas, but I was mostly the same person. Yet a year ago, someone like you probably would have had little interest in meeting someone like me."
    new "A year ago, I was on a fundamental level very much the same person that I am today, at my core. I've had new experiences since then, and changed some of my ideas, but I was mostly the same person. Yet a year ago, someone like you probably would have had little interest in meeting someone like me.\n一年前，在最根本的层面上，我内心深处和今天的我是同一个人。自那以后我有了新的经历，也改变了一些想法，但我大体上还是原来的我。然而一年前，像你这样的人，恐怕不会有兴趣见像我这样的人。"

    old "I would beg to differ, but you may be more right than I'd like to admit."
    new "I would beg to differ, but you may be more right than I'd like to admit.\n恕我不敢苟同，但你说得可能比我想承认的更在理。"

    old "What is it that's changed since then? It's not who I am inside that's changed. It's the things I've achieved."
    new "What is it that's changed since then? It's not who I am inside that's changed. It's the things I've achieved.\n自那以后，究竟改变了什么？改变的不是我内在的为人，而是我成就的那些事。"

    old "And you certainly have been busy."
    new "And you certainly have been busy.\n而你确实一直忙个不停。"

    old "I appreciate your willingness to engage in this exercise in self-reflection for my sake, [protag]."
    new "I appreciate your willingness to engage in this exercise in self-reflection for my sake, [protag].\n我很感激你愿意为了我而做这场自我反思的练习，[protag]。"

    old "Turnabout is fair play, isn't it? Don't I get to ask you questions?"
    new "Turnabout is fair play, isn't it? Don't I get to ask you questions?\n礼尚往来才公平，不是吗？难道不该轮到我问你问题了吗？"

    old "The purpose of asking someone questions is getting them to talk. And I think I've already said quite a lot to you, haven't I?"
    new "The purpose of asking someone questions is getting them to talk. And I think I've already said quite a lot to you, haven't I?\n向人提问的目的，是让对方开口。而我想，我已经对你说了不少了，不是吗？"

    old "In fact, we've been talking so long that I've nearly forgotten another engagement I have to attend to. I'm afraid I'll have to chase you away and ask to continue this conversation on another day. Hopefully you don't think me rude."
    new "In fact, we've been talking so long that I've nearly forgotten another engagement I have to attend to. I'm afraid I'll have to chase you away and ask to continue this conversation on another day. Hopefully you don't think me rude.\n事实上，我们聊得太久，我差点忘了自己还有另一个约会要赴。恐怕我得请你先走，改日再继续这场谈话了。希望你别觉得我失礼。"

    old "Until we meet again, then."
    new "Until we meet again, then.\n那就后会有期。"

    old "Lady Geraldine. I got your message."
    new "Lady Geraldine. I got your message.\nGeraldine 夫人。我收到了你的消息。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. I am glad you came. I have some news for you."
    new "Ah, [protag]. I am glad you came. I have some news for you.\n啊，[protag]。真高兴你来了。我有消息要告诉你。"

    old "Good news, I hope."
    new "Good news, I hope.\n我希望是好消息。"

    old "I'm afraid not. I have reason to believe someone is trying to betray me. Someone very close to me."
    new "I'm afraid not. I have reason to believe someone is trying to betray me. Someone very close to me.\n恐怕不是。我有理由相信，有人正想背叛我。一个与我非常亲近的人。"

    old "Ah. Now I understand why we've been meeting in the garden lately..."
    new "Ah. Now I understand why we've been meeting in the garden lately...\n啊。现在我明白为什么我们最近总是在花园里见面了……"

    old "It is as you suspect. I did not want to risk being overheard by anyone."
    new "It is as you suspect. I did not want to risk being overheard by anyone.\n正如你所料。我不想冒被任何人听到的风险。"

    old "...I'll be going away for some time, [protag]. I don't know for how long yet. Ten days... maybe more. I need to sort things out."
    new "...I'll be going away for some time, [protag]. I don't know for how long yet. Ten days... maybe more. I need to sort things out.\n……我要离开一段时间，[protag]。还不知道要多久。十天……也许更久。我需要把事情理清楚。"

    old "I see. And just how are you planning to do that?"
    new "I see. And just how are you planning to do that?\n我明白了。那你打算怎么理？"

    old "Nevermind the details. You have your own concerns at the moment. Just know that I will be reminding everyone that I am not someone that should be carelessly crossed."
    new "Nevermind the details. You have your own concerns at the moment. Just know that I will be reminding everyone that I am not someone that should be carelessly crossed.\n细节就别管了。你眼下有自己的事要操心。你只需知道，我会让所有人都明白，我不是那种可以随便招惹的人。"

    old "I don't inquire further. Lady Geraldine may seem like an ordinary noblewoman, but I'm certain that she can make good on that threat. I count myself lucky that I am not her enemy."
    new "I don't inquire further. Lady Geraldine may seem like an ordinary noblewoman, but I'm certain that she can make good on that threat. I count myself lucky that I am not her enemy.\n我没有再追问。Geraldine 夫人看起来或许像位寻常贵妇，但我确信她能让那句狠话兑现。我庆幸自己不是她的敌人。"

    old "In any event, I wanted to make sure that I wished you good luck on your mission in person before leaving."
    new "In any event, I wanted to make sure that I wished you good luck on your mission in person before leaving.\n无论如何，我想在离开之前，一定要当面向你道一声‘任务顺利’。"

    old "Thank you, Lady Geraldine. I'm flattered that you thought of me."
    new "Thank you, Lady Geraldine. I'm flattered that you thought of me.\n谢谢你，Geraldine 夫人。你能想到我，让我受宠若惊。"

    old "Lady Geraldine nods and then walks over to a nearby bush. She pulls a rapier out from behind it and then points it at me."
    new "Lady Geraldine nods and then walks over to a nearby bush. She pulls a rapier out from behind it and then points it at me.\nGeraldine 夫人点点头，然后走到旁边的一丛灌木前。她从灌木后面抽出一柄细剑，接着把剑指向了我。"

    old "Oh! Please, forgive me! I didn't think about how this might look to you. I meant only to offer it to you as a parting gift. Do you remember it? It is the rapier I showed you when we first met."
    new "Oh! Please, forgive me! I didn't think about how this might look to you. I meant only to offer it to you as a parting gift. Do you remember it? It is the rapier I showed you when we first met.\n哦！请原谅我！我没想过在你眼里这会是什么样。我只是想把它作为临别礼物送给你。你还记得吗？这是我们初识时我给你看过的那柄细剑。"

    old "Yes. I do recall that. It is truly a wonderful weapon."
    new "Yes. I do recall that. It is truly a wonderful weapon.\n记得。我确实记得。那真是一柄了不起的武器。"

    old "And now it is yours."
    new "And now it is yours.\n如今它归你了。"

    old "Are you sure? I... don't know what to say, Lady Geraldine."
    new "Are you sure? I... don't know what to say, Lady Geraldine.\n你确定吗？我……不知道说什么好，Geraldine 夫人。"

    old "Then say nothing. Win this fight for me too. That's all I ask of you."
    new "Then say nothing. Win this fight for me too. That's all I ask of you.\n那就什么都别说。这场仗，也替我打赢它。这是我对你唯一的请求。"

    old "Thank you. I will do my best."
    new "Thank you. I will do my best.\n谢谢你。我会竭尽全力。"

    old "Now, I am afraid it is time for the two of us to take our leave. When I return, I expect to find the N'Mar plains free of undead. They have been quite a disturbance. It will be nice to have my trading routes clear of them once more."
    new "Now, I am afraid it is time for the two of us to take our leave. When I return, I expect to find the N'Mar plains free of undead. They have been quite a disturbance. It will be nice to have my trading routes clear of them once more.\n现在，恐怕到了我们俩各自动身的时候了。等我回来时，我希望看到 N'Mar 平原不再有亡灵出没。它们实在是一大祸患。我的商路能再度畅通无阻，那可就太好了。"

    old "I can imagine. Hopefully when you get back, you'll be able to resume your business as if nothing happened."
    new "I can imagine. Hopefully when you get back, you'll be able to resume your business as if nothing happened.\n我能想象。希望你回来时，能像什么都没发生过一样，重新经营你的生意。"

    old "I would love that. Take care, [protag]."
    new "I would love that. Take care, [protag].\n那正是我所愿。保重，[protag]。"

    old "Goodbye, Lady Geraldine."
    new "Goodbye, Lady Geraldine.\n再会，Geraldine 夫人。"

    old "Apolimesho calls me to the council chambers for an 'important meeting.' Apolimesho isn't one to use such words lightly, so I make my way there with all due haste."
    new "Apolimesho calls me to the council chambers for an 'important meeting.' Apolimesho isn't one to use such words lightly, so I make my way there with all due haste.\nApolimesho 召我去议会厅，说有场‘重要会议’。Apolimesho 不是那种轻易用这种字眼的人，于是我火速赶了过去。"

    old "You wished to see me?"
    new "You wished to see me?\n你想见我？"

    old "Yes. I'm sure you don't need me to tell you this, but the council has been quite impressed with your performance so far. Your task force has far exceeded anyone's expectations. However..."
    new "Yes. I'm sure you don't need me to tell you this, but the council has been quite impressed with your performance so far. Your task force has far exceeded anyone's expectations. However...\n是的。我确信不用我多说，但议会对你至今的表现印象非常深刻。你的特遣队远远超出了所有人的预期。然而……"

    old "However?"
    new "However?\n然而？"

    old "The threat has exceeded our expectations as well. Your team is equipped to fight skirmishes, battles. But the council is in a position to consider the castle of N'Mar an existential threat to the entire Human Empire."
    new "The threat has exceeded our expectations as well. Your team is equipped to fight skirmishes, battles. But the council is in a position to consider the castle of N'Mar an existential threat to the entire Human Empire.\n威胁也同样超出了我们的预期。你的队伍足以应付小规模冲突和战斗。但议会现在不得不把 N'Mar 城堡视为对整个人类帝国的存亡威胁。"

    old "That sounds like exactly the kind of language I'd expect to hear on the eve of war."
    new "That sounds like exactly the kind of language I'd expect to hear on the eve of war.\n这听起来正是战争前夕我会料到的那种措辞。"

    old "That is exactly how the council feels about it, too. This is far beyond the capabilities of what your task force is capable of. This is war. Mighty though it may be, your group is small, and it is no way equipped for a full scale war if it comes to that."
    new "That is exactly how the council feels about it, too. This is far beyond the capabilities of what your task force is capable of. This is war. Mighty though it may be, your group is small, and it is no way equipped for a full scale war if it comes to that.\n议会对此也恰恰是这么看的。这远远超出了你的特遣队的能力范围。这是一场战争。你的队伍固然强悍，但人数太少，一旦真演变成全面战争，绝无应对之力。"

    old "Of course, this is what armies are for. But armies require resources."
    new "Of course, this is what armies are for. But armies require resources.\n当然，这正是军队的用武之地。但军队需要资源。"

    old "You mean money."
    new "You mean money.\n你是说钱。"

    old "Yes, that is one way to put it. Armies need to be supplied, both with materials and willing men. This ought to be the council's specialty. However, I think that perhaps your delicate touch might be necessary. And besides, you are the council's emissary. I think it's time that we send you on some official business."
    new "Yes, that is one way to put it. Armies need to be supplied, both with materials and willing men. This ought to be the council's specialty. However, I think that perhaps your delicate touch might be necessary. And besides, you are the council's emissary. I think it's time that we send you on some official business.\n是的，这是一种说法。军队需要补给，既要有物资，也要有肯卖命的人。这本该是议会的专长。不过我想，或许需要你那种细腻的手腕。况且，你是议会的使者。我想是时候派你去办些公务了。"

    old "What could I do that the council can't?"
    new "What could I do that the council can't?\n有什么是我能办而议会办不了的？"

    old "The council has...well, let's just say there are conflicts of interest at play here. Having you as a neutral third party would help settle things. I trust you would act impartially."
    new "The council has...well, let's just say there are conflicts of interest at play here. Having you as a neutral third party would help settle things. I trust you would act impartially.\n议会这边……这个嘛，就说这里有利益冲突在作祟吧。让你以中立的第三方身份介入，有助于把事情了结。我相信你会秉公行事。"

    old "I'll try to look at the facts objectively, then."
    new "I'll try to look at the facts objectively, then.\n那我尽量客观看待事实。"

    old "Yes, I thought to task you with this specifically because you are less likely to be swayed by bias."
    new "Yes, I thought to task you with this specifically because you are less likely to be swayed by bias.\n是的，我特意想把这差事交给你，正是因为你不太会被偏见左右。"

    old "I'll do whatever my gut tells me is right. I trust my instincts."
    new "I'll do whatever my gut tells me is right. I trust my instincts.\n我会凭直觉行事，做我认为对的事。我信任自己的直觉。"

    old "Coming from someone else, hearing those words might make me nervous. But given your accomplishments so far, I have no reason to doubt that your instincts will lead you in the right direction."
    new "Coming from someone else, hearing those words might make me nervous. But given your accomplishments so far, I have no reason to doubt that your instincts will lead you in the right direction.\n这话若出自别人之口，我听了或许会心里打鼓。但鉴于你迄今的成就，我没有理由怀疑你的直觉会把你引向正途。"

    old "So what exactly is it that you need me to settle?"
    new "So what exactly is it that you need me to settle?\n那么，你究竟需要我出面解决什么？"

    old "I'd like you to consider visiting the merchants of Lothark. I have two people in mind. One is a lady named Geraldine, who has deep ties to weapons manufacturers. Be it spears, axes, or broadswords, when it comes to mass-producing weapons, she has connections that would prove valuable."
    new "I'd like you to consider visiting the merchants of Lothark. I have two people in mind. One is a lady named Geraldine, who has deep ties to weapons manufacturers. Be it spears, axes, or broadswords, when it comes to mass-producing weapons, she has connections that would prove valuable.\n我希望你考虑去拜访 Lothark 的商人们。我心目中有人选两位。一位是名叫 Geraldine 的女士，她与武器制造商渊源颇深。无论是长矛、战斧还是阔剑，论大批量生产武器，她拥有的门路都价值非凡。"

    old "And the other person?"
    new "And the other person?\n另一位呢？"

    old "Sir Cedric. A veteran. He's well-respected by many military men, and as you might imagine, such a person would prove a valuable asset in times of war."
    new "Sir Cedric. A veteran. He's well-respected by many military men, and as you might imagine, such a person would prove a valuable asset in times of war.\nCedric 爵士。一位老兵。他深受许多军人敬重。你也能想到，这样的人在战时定会是一笔宝贵资产。"

    old "Is Sir Cedric a merchant or a military man?"
    new "Is Sir Cedric a merchant or a military man?\nCedric 爵士是商人还是军人？"

    old "People can be more than one thing, [protag]. He earned his reputation in his youth as a military officer, and when he aged beyond the point of being useful on a battlefield, he applied his leadership talents to commerce, winning a great fortune in the process."
    new "People can be more than one thing, [protag]. He earned his reputation in his youth as a military officer, and when he aged beyond the point of being useful on a battlefield, he applied his leadership talents to commerce, winning a great fortune in the process.\n人可以身兼多重身份，[protag]。他年轻时以军官身份赢得声望，待到年事渐高、再难在战场上出力时，他把自己的领导才能用到了经商上，并因此挣下了偌大家业。"

    old "Even though Cedric himself is not likely to be in a condition to serve as a battlefield commander, he's still a keen strategist, and his connections would no doubt prove valuable."
    new "Even though Cedric himself is not likely to be in a condition to serve as a battlefield commander, he's still a keen strategist, and his connections would no doubt prove valuable.\n尽管 Cedric 本人如今多半已不再适合担任战场指挥官，他仍是一位敏锐的战略家，他的人脉无疑也很有价值。"

    old "I guess I'm going to Lothark, then."
    new "I guess I'm going to Lothark, then.\n那看来我得去一趟 Lothark 了。"

    old "I was sure you'd agree, so I already informed Lady Geraldine that you would be visiting her soon."
    new "I was sure you'd agree, so I already informed Lady Geraldine that you would be visiting her soon.\n我料定你会同意，所以已经通知了 Geraldine 夫人，说你很快就会去拜访她。"

    old "You already set up an appointment?"
    new "You already set up an appointment?\n你已经安排好了会面？"

    old "Not an appointment, per se. I just passed along a message telling her to expect a visitor soon."
    new "Not an appointment, per se. I just passed along a message telling her to expect a visitor soon.\n严格说算不上安排会面。我只是传了个话，告诉她很快会有客人登门。"

    old "I guess I should visit her first, then."
    new "I guess I should visit her first, then.\n那我猜我应该先去拜访她。"

    old "[protag], one last thing. I'm afraid to inform you that the council cannot afford to give you 100 gold/day anymore. They've set the amount back to 50 gold/day."
    new "[protag], one last thing. I'm afraid to inform you that the council cannot afford to give you 100 gold/day anymore. They've set the amount back to 50 gold/day.\n[protag]，还有最后一件事。我不得不告诉你，议会再也负担不起每天给你 100 金币了。他们已把金额调回每天 50 金币。"

    old "What? If anything, I'd need more money now!"
    new "What? If anything, I'd need more money now!\n什么？要说起来，我现在明明需要更多钱啊！"

    old "I know, I know. Believe me, sometimes I wonder how we managed to survive for so long, when people in charge are only thinking about their own well-being."
    new "I know, I know. Believe me, sometimes I wonder how we managed to survive for so long, when people in charge are only thinking about their own well-being.\n我知道，我知道。相信我，有时候我也纳闷，当掌权者只顾着自己的利益时，我们是怎么撑到今天的。"

    old "Well, I suppose I'll have to accept their decision, as always."
    new "Well, I suppose I'll have to accept their decision, as always.\n唉，我想我不得不一如既往地接受他们的决定。"

    old "Lady Geraldine greets me at the gate with a faint but warm smile."
    new "Lady Geraldine greets me at the gate with a faint but warm smile.\nGeraldine 夫人在门口迎接我，脸上带着淡淡的、却温暖的笑意。"

    old "Emissary of Grimoire. Welcome. I apologize, you must be tiring of that title. What name should I address you by?"
    new "Emissary of Grimoire. Welcome. I apologize, you must be tiring of that title. What name should I address you by?\nGrimoire 的使者。欢迎光临。抱歉，你一定已经厌倦那个头衔了。我该怎么称呼你才好？"

    old "Geraldine clasps her hands together."
    new "Geraldine clasps her hands together.\nGeraldine 夫人双手合十。"

    old "[protag]. Wonderful. It's such a privilege to have the chance to talk with you about matters that are of such pressing importance. I trust you're here because of the business around the fields of N'Mar."
    new "[protag]. Wonderful. It's such a privilege to have the chance to talk with you about matters that are of such pressing importance. I trust you're here because of the business around the fields of N'Mar.\n[protag]。太好了。能有幸与你谈论如此要紧的大事，真是荣幸。我相信你此来，是为了 N'Mar 一带战事的事务吧。"

    old "Word I've heard is that you're in the process of assembling an army to take the castle by force, is that right?"
    new "Word I've heard is that you're in the process of assembling an army to take the castle by force, is that right?\n我听到的风声是，你正在集结一支军队，准备武力夺取城堡，对吗？"

    old "Right you are, my lady."
    new "Right you are, my lady.\n你说得没错，夫人。"

    old "It seems you already know my business. Where did your information come from?"
    new "It seems you already know my business. Where did your information come from?\n看来你已经知道我的来意了。你的消息从何而来？"

    old "Geraldine covers her mouth to conceal a smirk."
    new "Geraldine covers her mouth to conceal a smirk.\nGeraldine 夫人掩住嘴，藏起一抹得意的笑。"

    old "Why, you don't suppose I amassed my fortune from just good luck, do you? Information and friends are the true secret to any great merchant's success, and I don't think I'm any exception. Of course I have friends in Grimoire. Perhaps some day you'll be one of them."
    new "Why, you don't suppose I amassed my fortune from just good luck, do you? Information and friends are the true secret to any great merchant's success, and I don't think I'm any exception. Of course I have friends in Grimoire. Perhaps some day you'll be one of them.\n怎么，你该不会以为我的万贯家财只是靠好运气攒下的吧？情报和朋友，才是任何大商人成功的真正秘诀，我也不例外。我在 Grimoire 当然有朋友。也许有一天，你会成为其中之一。"

    old "Now, I imagine you'll be needing to outfit an army. Weapons, good weapons, finely tempered and ready for battle. That, I am prepared to provide."
    new "Now, I imagine you'll be needing to outfit an army. Weapons, good weapons, finely tempered and ready for battle. That, I am prepared to provide.\n现在，我想你需要武装一支军队。武器，精良的武器，锻造考究、随时可上战场。这些，我准备为你提供。"

    old "I came here with that expectation. I was hoping to discuss terms of payment. Grimoire is not exactly flush with capital at the moment."
    new "I came here with that expectation. I was hoping to discuss terms of payment. Grimoire is not exactly flush with capital at the moment.\n我正是带着这份期望来的。我本想与你谈谈付款条件。Grimoire 眼下手头的资金并不宽裕。"

    old "I understand that times of war can be financially trying, and I am prepared to offer you use of weapons on credit. If you fight at N'mar and lose, then you pay nothing."
    new "I understand that times of war can be financially trying, and I am prepared to offer you use of weapons on credit. If you fight at N'mar and lose, then you pay nothing.\n我明白战时财政吃紧，因此我准备以赊账的方式供你使用武器。如果你在 N'Mar 作战而败，那你分文不付。"

    old "And if we win?"
    new "And if we win?\n那如果我们赢了呢？"

    old "Then you will pay the normal rate for the weapons and supplies you use, plus twenty percent."
    new "Then you will pay the normal rate for the weapons and supplies you use, plus twenty percent.\n那你就按正常价格支付你所用的武器和补给，另加两成。"

    old "That's a significant mark-up."
    new "That's a significant mark-up.\n这加价可不小。"

    old "Is it, though? Think of it this way. Paying for supplies now would break the bank for Grimoire's council. But if you successfully take N'mar, to you will go the spoils of war."
    new "Is it, though? Think of it this way. Paying for supplies now would break the bank for Grimoire's council. But if you successfully take N'mar, to you will go the spoils of war.\n是吗？换个角度想。现在付补给的钱，会让 Grimoire 议会倾家荡产。可如果你成功拿下 N'Mar，战利品就归你了。"

    old "I don't know what riches lie within that castle, but they must be substantial. Paying the extra amount for the weapons would be trivial with whatever riches you find there. And you also lessen your risk of devastating loss, for if you fail in battle, I will shoulder the material loss of supplies."
    new "I don't know what riches lie within that castle, but they must be substantial. Paying the extra amount for the weapons would be trivial with whatever riches you find there. And you also lessen your risk of devastating loss, for if you fail in battle, I will shoulder the material loss of supplies.\n我不知道那城堡里藏着什么财宝，但想必颇为可观。用你在那里找到的财宝来支付武器的加价，不过是九牛一毛。而且你还降低了惨重损失的风险——因为一旦你战败，补给的物资损失由我承担。"

    old "You benefit in either case. And this arrangement would also allow you to hold me accountable as well, because I'd have a vested interest in ensuring Grimoire's success in battle."
    new "You benefit in either case. And this arrangement would also allow you to hold me accountable as well, because I'd have a vested interest in ensuring Grimoire's success in battle.\n无论如何你都有利可图。而这样的安排也能让你反过来盯紧我，因为确保 Grimoire 在战场上取胜，关乎我的切身利益。"

    old "So you're saying that you want a stake in the outcome of our battle?"
    new "So you're saying that you want a stake in the outcome of our battle?\n所以你是说，你想在我们这场仗的胜负里分一杯羹？"

    old "That's exactly right. I want to invest in your war effort."
    new "That's exactly right. I want to invest in your war effort.\n正是如此。我想投资你的战事。"

    old "Those are terms I'm sure the council will agree to. If we win, paying you an additional percentage should be no problem. And while I don't like to think that we will lose, having that contingency partially prepared will be advantageous."
    new "Those are terms I'm sure the council will agree to. If we win, paying you an additional percentage should be no problem. And while I don't like to think that we will lose, having that contingency partially prepared will be advantageous.\n这些条件，我相信议会一定会同意。如果我们赢了，多付你一些百分比不成问题。虽然我不愿去想我们会输，但把这种不测预先做些安排，总归有利。"

    old "Excellent. There's another matter I'd like to discuss as well. It pertains to the subject of the weaponry."
    new "Excellent. There's another matter I'd like to discuss as well. It pertains to the subject of the weaponry.\n很好。还有另一件事我也想谈谈。它与武器本身有关。"

    old "What is there to discuss?"
    new "What is there to discuss?\n还有什么可谈的？"

    old "I follow Lady Geraldine as she enters her mansion. The luxury of the furniture reflects her social status."
    new "I follow Lady Geraldine as she enters her mansion. The luxury of the furniture reflects her social status.\n我跟随 Geraldine 夫人走进她的宅邸。家具的奢华，处处映衬着她的社会地位。"

    old "I'm prepared to offer you iron weapons. Those, we have access to in great abundance. But there may also be an opportunity to offer you something much better. Steel weapons."
    new "I'm prepared to offer you iron weapons. Those, we have access to in great abundance. But there may also be an opportunity to offer you something much better. Steel weapons.\n我准备向你提供铁制武器。这些我们货源充足。但或许还有个机会，能向你提供好得多的东西——钢制武器。"

    old "What exactly is the difference between iron and steel?"
    new "What exactly is the difference between iron and steel?\n铁和钢到底有什么区别？"

    old "Steel is an alloy forged from iron that offers much greater strength. Steel is harder, and much more durable. There is much less chance of a steel breastplate being penetrated or a steel blade snapping in the midst of battle."
    new "Steel is an alloy forged from iron that offers much greater strength. Steel is harder, and much more durable. There is much less chance of a steel breastplate being penetrated or a steel blade snapping in the midst of battle.\n钢是由铁锻造而成的合金，强度远胜于铁。钢更坚硬，也更耐用。钢制胸甲被击穿、或钢刃在激战中折断的几率都要小得多。"

    old "Not only that, but steel weapons and armor are much lighter than their iron counterparts. I'm sure you know what that means. Greater ease of movement, less fatigue, and greater speed on the battlefield."
    new "Not only that, but steel weapons and armor are much lighter than their iron counterparts. I'm sure you know what that means. Greater ease of movement, less fatigue, and greater speed on the battlefield.\n不仅如此，钢制武器和盔甲比同类的铁制品轻得多。我确信你明白这意味着什么——行动更自如，更不易疲惫，在战场上速度更快。"

    old "Are there any drawbacks to steel weapons?"
    new "Are there any drawbacks to steel weapons?\n钢制武器有什么缺点吗？"

    old "None whatsoever when it comes to battlefield utility. But there is the issue of manufacturing."
    new "None whatsoever when it comes to battlefield utility. But there is the issue of manufacturing.\n论战场效用，一点缺点都没有。但制造上倒有个问题。"

    old "Crafting steel is a fine art. Not just any blacksmith can make a steel sword. It takes a skilled metalworker to properly temper steel. And the metalworkers' guild has gone on strike."
    new "Crafting steel is a fine art. Not just any blacksmith can make a steel sword. It takes a skilled metalworker to properly temper steel. And the metalworkers' guild has gone on strike.\n炼钢是一门精妙的手艺。不是随便哪个铁匠都能打造钢剑。要把钢淬炼得当，需要技艺娴熟的金属工匠。而金属工匠行会已经罢工了。"

    old "Things have gotten political?"
    new "Things have gotten political?\n事情变得政治化了？"

    old "Indeed they have."
    new "Indeed they have.\n确实如此。"

    old "Politics, eh? Sounds like my area of expertise."
    new "Politics, eh? Sounds like my area of expertise.\n政治，嗯？听起来正撞上我的专长。"

    old "I'm glad to hear you think so."
    new "I'm glad to hear you think so.\n听你这么说，我很高兴。"

    old "Why don't you fill me in on the particulars of this strike."
    new "Why don't you fill me in on the particulars of this strike.\n你不妨把这次罢工的详情给我讲讲。"

    old "Politics, eh? Not really my cup of tea."
    new "Politics, eh? Not really my cup of tea.\n政治，嗯？我可不太感冒。"

    old "Well, if you detest politics, I think you're serving in the wrong profession. After all, you do represent the council of Grimoire."
    new "Well, if you detest politics, I think you're serving in the wrong profession. After all, you do represent the council of Grimoire.\n哦，如果你厌恶政治，我想你是入错了行。毕竟，你代表的可是 Grimoire 议会。"

    old "I'm an instrument of the council's will. They bend me to suit their purposes."
    new "I'm an instrument of the council's will. They bend me to suit their purposes.\n我是议会意志的工具。他们让我屈从于他们的目的。"

    old "I wish you wouldn't be so modest. It's plain to me that you're no simple messenger. You have a voice among those at Grimoire, and I suspect that you wield more influence than you may realize."
    new "I wish you wouldn't be so modest. It's plain to me that you're no simple messenger. You have a voice among those at Grimoire, and I suspect that you wield more influence than you may realize.\n希望你别这么谦虚。我看得清清楚楚，你绝不只是个跑腿的信使。在 Grimoire 那些人中间，你有发言权，而且我怀疑你拥有的影响力比你意识到的更大。"

    old "I've heard of your exploits. You've been parlaying with groups all across Aravorn. Most emissaries don't wield that kind of autonomy. Like it or not, you're a political entity."
    new "I've heard of your exploits. You've been parlaying with groups all across Aravorn. Most emissaries don't wield that kind of autonomy. Like it or not, you're a political entity.\n我听说过你的壮举。你一直在 Aravorn 各地与各方势力交涉。大多数使者可没有这么大的自主权。不管你喜不喜欢，你都是一个政治实体。"

    old "I've little taste for politics, but you may be right. What exactly do I need to know about this situation? You said something about metalworkers on strike?"
    new "I've little taste for politics, but you may be right. What exactly do I need to know about this situation? You said something about metalworkers on strike?\n我对政治兴致缺缺，但也许你说得对。这个局面，我究竟需要了解些什么？你刚提到了金属工匠罢工？"

    old "Geraldine smiles and offers a shrug."
    new "Geraldine smiles and offers a shrug.\nGeraldine 夫人笑了笑，耸了耸肩。"

    old "What is any strike about? They want higher pay and better working conditions."
    new "What is any strike about? They want higher pay and better working conditions.\n任何罢工还不都是那么回事？他们想要更高的报酬和更好的工作条件。"

    old "Workers always want better pay and conditions. What worker wouldn't? The question is, what drove them to try and collectively bargain?"
    new "Workers always want better pay and conditions. What worker wouldn't? The question is, what drove them to try and collectively bargain?\n工人总想要更好的报酬和条件。哪个工人不想呢？问题在于，是什么促使他们试图集体谈判？"

    old "These aren't your typical workers. They represent the most skilled in their craft, and they're looking to collectively take ownership of their own output."
    new "These aren't your typical workers. They represent the most skilled in their craft, and they're looking to collectively take ownership of their own output.\n他们可不是普通的工人。他们代表着本行当中手艺最精湛的一批人，而他们想要集体拥有自己的产出。"

    old "So they're businessmen as well as craftsmen."
    new "So they're businessmen as well as craftsmen.\n所以他们既是工匠，也是商人。"

    old "That's their goal. They just need a facility of their own. A facility grand enough to support the best and brightest of the craft."
    new "That's their goal. They just need a facility of their own. A facility grand enough to support the best and brightest of the craft.\n这正是他们的目标。他们只缺一处属于自己的工坊——一处宏大得足以容纳这行当中最优秀、最杰出人才的工坊。"

    old "How close are they to making that facility?"
    new "How close are they to making that facility?\n他们离建成那处工坊还有多远？"

    old "They have the capital and they're ready to build. But they haven't purchased the land yet, and that's where we've run into problems."
    new "They have the capital and they're ready to build. But they haven't purchased the land yet, and that's where we've run into problems.\n资金已经有了，也随时可以开工。只是他们还没买下地皮，问题就出在这里。"

    old "There's a prime piece of real estate that is ideal for metalworking. It's located on the river, which makes it an advantageous location as part of a larger supply chain. And being on the river also allows for the use of water-powered tools."
    new "There's a prime piece of real estate that is ideal for metalworking. It's located on the river, which makes it an advantageous location as part of a larger supply chain. And being on the river also allows for the use of water-powered tools.\n有一块上等地产，极适合做金属加工。它坐落在河畔，作为更庞大供应链的一环，位置得天独厚。临河还能利用水力驱动的工具。"

    old "Furthermore, it's located on the crest of the hill, giving it ideal air circulation as well. It makes for much more efficient cooling, and it's also makes the working conditions a great deal more pleasant as well."
    new "Furthermore, it's located on the crest of the hill, giving it ideal air circulation as well. It makes for much more efficient cooling, and it's also makes the working conditions a great deal more pleasant as well.\n此外，它位于山丘之巅，通风也极为理想。这既能让冷却效率高得多，也让工作条件舒适得多。"

    old "There's just a small issue. That land happens to be the location of an old war monument."
    new "There's just a small issue. That land happens to be the location of an old war monument.\n只是有个小问题。那块地恰好是一座旧战争纪念碑的所在地。"

    old "You mean the tribute on the hill?"
    new "You mean the tribute on the hill?\n你是指山上的那座纪念碑？"

    old "That's the one. The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier."
    new "That's the one. The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier.\n就是那座。Tomb of the Unknown Soldier。"

    old "That monument is a historic landmark."
    new "That monument is a historic landmark.\n那座纪念碑是一处历史地标。"

    old "You can't plow over a military monument without facing some resistance."
    new "You can't plow over a military monument without facing some resistance.\n你不可能铲平一座军事纪念碑而不遇到阻力。"

    old "Hence the political struggle. Some military veterans, most of them retired officers, don't take kindly to the notion of replacing a war memorial with a workshop. Do you want to know what I think?"
    new "Hence the political struggle. Some military veterans, most of them retired officers, don't take kindly to the notion of replacing a war memorial with a workshop. Do you want to know what I think?\n于是便有了这场政治角力。一些退伍军人——其中大多是退役军官——对用工坊取代战争纪念碑的念头颇为不满。你想知道我的看法吗？"

    old "Tell me."
    new "Tell me.\n说来听听。"

    old "The needs of the living outweigh the needs of the dead. Give the dead their respect. But don't let them occupy space that could be put to better use. The memorial can always be rebuilt elsewhere."
    new "The needs of the living outweigh the needs of the dead. Give the dead their respect. But don't let them occupy space that could be put to better use. The memorial can always be rebuilt elsewhere.\n生者的需求重于逝者。逝者自当尊重，但别让他们占据本可派上更大用场的空间。纪念碑总可以在别处重建。"

    old "I agree. But I'm afraid the military veterans won't see it the same way."
    new "I agree. But I'm afraid the military veterans won't see it the same way.\n我同意。但恐怕退伍军人们不会这么看。"

    old "And this troubles you?"
    new "And this troubles you?\n这让你困扰吗？"

    old "I'm preparing to fight a war. It behooves me to consider how veteran officers might feel about the matter. I'd rather have them as friends than allies."
    new "I'm preparing to fight a war. It behooves me to consider how veteran officers might feel about the matter. I'd rather have them as friends than allies.\n我正准备打仗。理应顾及退伍军官们对此事的感受。我宁愿他们做我的朋友，而不是仅做盟友。"

    old "I wish I could agree with you. But there are some things that are sacred. That war memorial is one of them."
    new "I wish I could agree with you. But there are some things that are sacred. That war memorial is one of them.\n但愿我能同意你。但有些东西是神圣的。那座战争纪念碑就是其中之一。"

    old "Why is that memorial so important to you?"
    new "Why is that memorial so important to you?\n那座纪念碑为何对你如此重要？"

    old "It's built to respect soldiers who sacrificed their lives in military service. And as someone preparing to fight a war, I think I ought to have more than a little respect for that."
    new "It's built to respect soldiers who sacrificed their lives in military service. And as someone preparing to fight a war, I think I ought to have more than a little respect for that.\n它是为敬重那些在军旅中献出生命的将士而建。而作为一个正准备打仗的人，我想我理应对此怀有不止一点敬意。"

    old "[protag], have you thought about how you're going to win this war?"
    new "[protag], have you thought about how you're going to win this war?\n[protag]，你想过要怎么打赢这场战争吗？"

    old "Of course I have. What are you getting at?"
    new "Of course I have. What are you getting at?\n当然想过。你想说什么？"

    old "Grimoire is not a city of fighters. You don't have a standing military that can stand up to the task of invading a castle. You're going to be relying on conscripts. This is a battle that will be won by commoners, armed with whatever weapons you can scramble together. And that's not something to be afraid of."
    new "Grimoire is not a city of fighters. You don't have a standing military that can stand up to the task of invading a castle. You're going to be relying on conscripts. This is a battle that will be won by commoners, armed with whatever weapons you can scramble together. And that's not something to be afraid of.\nGrimoire 不是一座善战之城。你们没有能胜任攻城任务的常备军。你们将倚仗被征召的平民。这场仗，要靠拿着你们东拼西凑来的武器的普通人去打赢。而这没什么可怕的。"

    old "[protag], do you know what I love about technology?"
    new "[protag], do you know what I love about technology?\n[protag]，你知道我喜欢技术哪一点吗？"

    old "Look at this axe on the wall."
    new "Look at this axe on the wall.\n看看墙上这把斧子。"

    old "Geraldine points to a bronze axe with a long wooden handle, hanging from two pegs on the wall."
    new "Geraldine points to a bronze axe with a long wooden handle, hanging from two pegs on the wall.\nGeraldine 夫人指着一把青铜斧，斧柄是长长的木柄，挂在墙上两枚木钉之间。"

    old "Would you like to try and heft it?"
    new "Would you like to try and heft it?\n你想不想试着掂一掂它？"

    old "I place both hands on the wooden handle, and lift the axe from where it rests. I test the axe with both hands."
    new "I place both hands on the wooden handle, and lift the axe from where it rests. I test the axe with both hands.\n我双手握住木柄，把斧子从它搁着的地方提起来，用两只手试了试分量。"

    old "Do you think a woman of my stature could ever hope to wield such a weapon?"
    new "Do you think a woman of my stature could ever hope to wield such a weapon?\n你觉得，像我这般身量的女人，有朝一日能指望舞动这样的武器吗？"

    old "Yes. Yes, I think you could."
    new "Yes. Yes, I think you could.\n能。是的，我觉得你能。"

    old "Come now, don't flatter me. With a bit of effort, I might have a chance at holding the weapon in my hands and giving a few swings without dropping it, but you know perfectly well that wielding such a brutish weapon in combat is far beyond my capability."
    new "Come now, don't flatter me. With a bit of effort, I might have a chance at holding the weapon in my hands and giving a few swings without dropping it, but you know perfectly well that wielding such a brutish weapon in combat is far beyond my capability.\n得了，别奉承我。费点力气，我也许还能把武器握在手里，抡上几下而不脱手，但你心里清楚得很，在战斗中舞动如此笨重的武器，远远超出了我的能力。"

    old "I'd be utterly useless armed with such a weapon. Training a woman of my age and stature in the use of a bronze axe would be futile."
    new "I'd be utterly useless armed with such a weapon. Training a woman of my age and stature in the use of a bronze axe would be futile.\n拿着这样的武器，我会毫无用处。训练一个像我这般年纪、这般身量的女人使用青铜斧，纯属徒劳。"

    old "Do you think that strong warriors are born with giant rippling muscles? They worked to achieve that physique. Training for that role is an arduous process, but it's not futile."
    new "Do you think that strong warriors are born with giant rippling muscles? They worked to achieve that physique. Training for that role is an arduous process, but it's not futile.\n你以为强壮的战士天生就有一身贲张的肌肉吗？那是他们为练就那副体魄流汗换来的。为那个角色而训练，是个艰辛的过程，但绝非徒劳。"

    old "I'm not trying to discount the importance of pigheaded determination. Of course strong warriors work to achieve their level of combat readiness. But each one of us is born with certain attributes. I will never have the strength of a six-foot tall bruiser, no matter how much I train."
    new "I'm not trying to discount the importance of pigheaded determination. Of course strong warriors work to achieve their level of combat readiness. But each one of us is born with certain attributes. I will never have the strength of a six-foot tall bruiser, no matter how much I train.\n我无意贬低那股倔强决心的分量。当然，强壮的战士都靠苦练达到自己的临战水准。但我们每个人天生禀赋不同。无论我怎么练，也永远不会有六尺壮汉那样的力气。"

    old "No, I don't suppose you could."
    new "No, I don't suppose you could.\n不，我想你也不会有。"

    old "Of course, that much should be obvious."
    new "Of course, that much should be obvious.\n当然，这一点本该显而易见。"

    old "Now, take a look at this."
    new "Now, take a look at this.\n现在，看看这个。"

    old "Geraldine walks over to the wall, and picks up a display piece."
    new "Geraldine walks over to the wall, and picks up a display piece.\nGeraldine 夫人走到墙边，拿起一件展示品。"

    old "Look at this rapier."
    new "Look at this rapier.\n看看这柄细剑。"

    old "It looks beautiful."
    new "It looks beautiful.\n它看起来很美。"

    old "It is, isn't it? The design is quite striking, but it doesn't sacrifice practicality."
    new "It is, isn't it? The design is quite striking, but it doesn't sacrifice practicality.\n很美，对吧？设计相当夺目，却丝毫不牺牲实用性。"

    old "The handle may appear overly ornate, but it also serves the very practical function of concentrating the weapon's weight near the hilt of the weapon. The etched patterns also serve as a comfortable grip. The hilt itself is designed to protect the hand, making it a perfect dueling weapon."
    new "The handle may appear overly ornate, but it also serves the very practical function of concentrating the weapon's weight near the hilt of the weapon. The etched patterns also serve as a comfortable grip. The hilt itself is designed to protect the hand, making it a perfect dueling weapon.\n剑柄看起来或许过于华丽，但它也承担着极其实用的功能——把武器的重量集中在剑柄附近。蚀刻的花纹也便于握持。护手本身的设计就是为了保护手部，使它成为一柄完美的决斗武器。"

    old "There's something wonderfully elegant about a weapon designed for practical use, something that the finest painter or sculptor could never hope to match."
    new "There's something wonderfully elegant about a weapon designed for practical use, something that the finest painter or sculptor could never hope to match.\n为实战而设计的武器，自有种美妙绝伦的优雅，那是再出色的画家或雕塑家也永远无法企及的。"

    old "It looks light."
    new "It looks light.\n它看起来很轻。"

    old "Geraldine smiles and hefts the weapon."
    new "Geraldine smiles and hefts the weapon.\nGeraldine 夫人微笑着把武器掂了掂。"

    old "Light indeed. It's actually deceptively light, in fact. The weapon in whole weighs nearly two pounds, but most of the weight is concentrated at the hilt. It's almost the reverse of an axe, which has most of the weight concentrated in the metal head."
    new "Light indeed. It's actually deceptively light, in fact. The weapon in whole weighs nearly two pounds, but most of the weight is concentrated at the hilt. It's almost the reverse of an axe, which has most of the weight concentrated in the metal head.\n确实轻。事实上，它轻得出人意料。整件武器重近两磅，但大部分重量都集中在剑柄处。这几乎与斧子正好相反——斧子的大部分重量都集中在金属斧头上。"

    old "That property of weight makes the rapier ideal for thrusting. The hilt, while it may appear overly ornamental, actually serves the practical function of protecting the hand. If there exists a perfect dueling weapon, you're looking at it right now."
    new "That property of weight makes the rapier ideal for thrusting. The hilt, while it may appear overly ornamental, actually serves the practical function of protecting the hand. If there exists a perfect dueling weapon, you're looking at it right now.\n这种重量分布使细剑极适合突刺。护手虽然看似过于装饰，实际却承担着保护手部的实用功能。如果世上真有完美的决斗武器，那么此刻你正看着它。"

    old "It looks deadly."
    new "It looks deadly.\n它看起来很致命。"

    old "Geraldine smiles and nods."
    new "Geraldine smiles and nods.\nGeraldine 夫人微笑着点点头。"

    old "Deadly indeed, and in a lightweight package. This is a weapon built combat. The beauty of the hilt's design belies this weapon's brutal efficiency as a tool for killing."
    new "Deadly indeed, and in a lightweight package. This is a weapon built combat. The beauty of the hilt's design belies this weapon's brutal efficiency as a tool for killing.\n确实致命，而且轻巧便携。这是一件为战斗而生的武器。剑柄设计之美，掩盖不了它作为杀戮工具那残酷的高效。"

    old "In fact, the design of the hilt and handle serves the function of concentrating the weapon's weight in or around the hand of the person wielding it. The hilt also protects the bearer's hand, making it an ideal weapon for dueling."
    new "In fact, the design of the hilt and handle serves the function of concentrating the weapon's weight in or around the hand of the person wielding it. The hilt also protects the bearer's hand, making it an ideal weapon for dueling.\n事实上，剑柄与握把的设计，起着把武器重量集中于持剑者手部或手部附近的作用。护手还保护持剑者的手，使它成为理想的决斗武器。"

    old "Stand back, will you?"
    new "Stand back, will you?\n退后一点，好吗？"

    old "I back up and give Geraldine a wide berth."
    new "I back up and give Geraldine a wide berth.\n我后退几步，给 Geraldine 夫人让出空间。"

    old "Geraldine grasps the rapier and levels it horizontally, then delivers three swift thrusts in rapid succession. She follows the last thrust with a series of slashes before returning the blade to a defensive position, as if ready to parry."
    new "Geraldine grasps the rapier and levels it horizontally, then delivers three swift thrusts in rapid succession. She follows the last thrust with a series of slashes before returning the blade to a defensive position, as if ready to parry.\nGeraldine 夫人握紧细剑，横剑平举，随后接连刺出三记快刺。最后一刺过后，她又跟上一连串劈砍，接着收剑回到防御架势，仿佛随时准备格挡。"

    old "Impressive, for a merchant."
    new "Impressive, for a merchant.\n对一个商人来说，真了不起。"

    old "You never told me you were a duelist."
    new "You never told me you were a duelist.\n你从没告诉过我，你竟是位决斗者。"

    old "I'm no duelist. Not a competent one, at any rate. I scarcely qualify as a novice, though if time permits I would very much like to take the time to practice more. I merely wished to demonstrate a point."
    new "I'm no duelist. Not a competent one, at any rate. I scarcely qualify as a novice, though if time permits I would very much like to take the time to practice more. I merely wished to demonstrate a point.\n我可不是什么决斗者。至少算不上合格的。我连新手都勉强，不过时间允许的话，我倒很愿意多花时间练习。我方才只是想说明一点。"

    old "The rapier is a much newer invention, compared to the battle axe. Do you know why that is?"
    new "The rapier is a much newer invention, compared to the battle axe. Do you know why that is?\n与战斧相比，细剑是晚得多的发明。你知道这是为什么吗？"

    old "The rapier is a weapon that requires discipline to use. Primitive warriors lacked the skill to wield such a weapon. The brutish battle axe is a weapon better suited to a less civilized age."
    new "The rapier is a weapon that requires discipline to use. Primitive warriors lacked the skill to wield such a weapon. The brutish battle axe is a weapon better suited to a less civilized age.\n细剑是一种需靠修习才能使用的武器。原始战士缺乏舞动这类武器的技艺。笨重的战斧，则是更适合蒙昧时代的武器。"

    old "You are partly correct. The rapier was designed as a weapon for dueling. In a way, it can be seen as an evolution of the sword. But the simpler reason is that previous generations simply lacked the ability to forge a weapon as fine as the rapier."
    new "You are partly correct. The rapier was designed as a weapon for dueling. In a way, it can be seen as an evolution of the sword. But the simpler reason is that previous generations simply lacked the ability to forge a weapon as fine as the rapier.\n你说对了一部分。细剑是作为决斗武器设计的。从某种角度看，它可以被视为剑的演化。但更简单的原因在于，前人根本没有能力锻造出细剑这般精良的武器。"

    old "This rapier is cut from a finer cloth. Or to be more accurate, forged from a finer metal."
    new "This rapier is cut from a finer cloth. Or to be more accurate, forged from a finer metal.\n这柄细剑用的是上等料子。更准确地说，是用更精良的金属锻造而成。"

    old "Right you are."
    new "Right you are.\n说得没错。"

    old "There's a reason that the only rapiers you'll ever see are those forged from steel. Look at this blade."
    new "There's a reason that the only rapiers you'll ever see are those forged from steel. Look at this blade.\n你见到的细剑无一不是钢制，这是有原因的。看看这剑身。"

    old "Geraldine holds the rapier up for me to see."
    new "Geraldine holds the rapier up for me to see.\nGeraldine 夫人举起细剑，让我看清。"

    old "It's thin enough to be used as a thrusting weapon, but with a sharp edge that can be used for slashing. Try forging a blade like this from bronze, and you'll never have an edge that sharp. Try it with iron, and a blade this thin would be too frail to hold up in combat."
    new "It's thin enough to be used as a thrusting weapon, but with a sharp edge that can be used for slashing. Try forging a blade like this from bronze, and you'll never have an edge that sharp. Try it with iron, and a blade this thin would be too frail to hold up in combat.\n它薄得足以用作突刺，却又带着可用于劈砍的利刃。你试试用青铜锻造这样的剑身，永远磨不出那么锋利的刃口。改用铁来试，这么薄的剑身又太脆，撑不过实战。"

    old "And in any case, the light weight of steel is what makes it possible to have a blade this long yet light enough for someone like me to thrust or slash with it."
    new "And in any case, the light weight of steel is what makes it possible to have a blade this long yet light enough for someone like me to thrust or slash with it.\n而无论如何，钢的轻巧，才使得剑身能做到这般长，却又轻得足以让我这样的人用它突刺或劈砍。"

    old "A steel rapier is a wonderful thing. It doesn't matter if you're a gigantic lumberjack who weighs 15 stone, or a meek adolescent who is a scribe by trade."
    new "A steel rapier is a wonderful thing. It doesn't matter if you're a gigantic lumberjack who weighs 15 stone, or a meek adolescent who is a scribe by trade.\n一柄钢制细剑是件奇妙的东西。无论你是重达十五石的高大伐木工，还是个以抄写为业的文弱少年，都无关紧要。"

    old "Egalitarianism at its finest. That is the true power of technology."
    new "Egalitarianism at its finest. That is the true power of technology.\n平等主义的最佳体现。这才是技术的真正力量。"

    old "Geraldine returns the rapier to its display hooks on the wall."
    new "Geraldine returns the rapier to its display hooks on the wall.\nGeraldine 夫人把细剑放回墙上的展示挂钩。"

    old "When you look at this blade, I hope that you see more than just a weapon. It's not merely a tool for fighting. It's a tool for social justice."
    new "When you look at this blade, I hope that you see more than just a weapon. It's not merely a tool for fighting. It's a tool for social justice.\n当你看着这剑身时，我希望你看到的不只是一件武器。它不只是战斗的工具，更是社会正义的工具。"

    old "That's an admirable stance to take."
    new "That's an admirable stance to take.\n这是个令人钦佩的立场。"

    old "That's interesting to hear from someone in a position like yours."
    new "That's interesting to hear from someone in a position like yours.\n这话从你这种地位的人口中说出，倒是有趣。"

    old "That's certainly not the kind of message I expected to hear when I came here."
    new "That's certainly not the kind of message I expected to hear when I came here.\n这确实不是我此来想听到的那类论调。"

    old "I'm not sure I know what you mean."
    new "I'm not sure I know what you mean.\n我不太明白你的意思。"

    old "I just meant that it seems odd for a an affluent person such as yourself to have such strong views on equality."
    new "I just meant that it seems odd for a an affluent person such as yourself to have such strong views on equality.\n我只是想说，像你这样富裕的人，对平等竟有如此强烈的看法，似乎有些奇怪。"

    old "People will surprise you if you give them the chance. I hope I still have a few surprises in store for you."
    new "People will surprise you if you give them the chance. I hope I still have a few surprises in store for you.\n你若肯给人们机会，他们会让你刮目相看。我希望我还留着几手惊喜给你。"

    old "I'm what you might call 'new money.' I made my fortune, and I owe that privilege largely to the meritocratic nature of my trade. A merchant is judged only by markets."
    new "I'm what you might call 'new money.' I made my fortune, and I owe that privilege largely to the meritocratic nature of my trade. A merchant is judged only by markets.\n我就是你们说的‘新贵’。我靠自己发家，而这份殊荣很大程度上要归功于我这行当的唯才是举。商人，只由市场来评判。"

    old "Spend some more time among the merchants of Lothark, and you might learn a thing or two about what it means to build a fortune through merit."
    new "Spend some more time among the merchants of Lothark, and you might learn a thing or two about what it means to build a fortune through merit.\n在 Lothark 的商人堆里多待些时日，你或许就能略懂一二——凭本事发家意味着什么。"

    old "You've given me a lot to think about."
    new "You've given me a lot to think about.\n你给了我许多值得思考的东西。"

    old "Of course. I don't expect you to make your decision on the matter of the metalworkers' strike immediately. Take some time to consider what the consequences of your actions will be."
    new "Of course. I don't expect you to make your decision on the matter of the metalworkers' strike immediately. Take some time to consider what the consequences of your actions will be.\n当然。我不指望你立刻就对金属工匠罢工一事做出决定。花些时间，想想你的行动会带来什么后果。"

    old "I arrive at Cedric's estate. A page escorts me to his drawing room and he arrives without much delay."
    new "I arrive at Cedric's estate. A page escorts me to his drawing room and he arrives without much delay.\n我抵达 Cedric 的宅邸。一名侍从把我领进他的会客厅，他没过多久就到了。"

    old "Sir Cedric, thank you for taking the time to meet with me."
    new "Sir Cedric, thank you for taking the time to meet with me.\nCedric 爵士，感谢你抽出时间与我见面。"

    old "I appreciate the 'Sir,' but the formality isn't needed here. You're not serving under me, and besides that, this meeting is very unofficial. 'Cedric' will do just fine."
    new "I appreciate the 'Sir,' but the formality isn't needed here. You're not serving under me, and besides that, this meeting is very unofficial. 'Cedric' will do just fine.\n多谢你称我一声‘爵士’，但这里不必拘礼。你又不是我麾下，何况这次会面本就很随意。叫我‘Cedric’就好。"

    old "Now, I understand you come bringing a request from Grimoire's elders."
    new "Now, I understand you come bringing a request from Grimoire's elders.\n那么，我听说你是带着 Grimoire 长者们的请求而来。"

    old "Yes. Are you already aware of the business around the fields of N'Mar?"
    new "Yes. Are you already aware of the business around the fields of N'Mar?\n是的。N'Mar 一带的战事，你已经知晓了吗？"

    old "A man in my position has to stay well-informed. I suspect that I know as much about Grimoire's tactical situation as anyone on the council."
    new "A man in my position has to stay well-informed. I suspect that I know as much about Grimoire's tactical situation as anyone on the council.\n处在我这个位置上的人，必须消息灵通。我猜我对 Grimoire 战局态势的了解，不亚于议会里任何一位。"

    old "Then you know about our need to prepare for battle."
    new "Then you know about our need to prepare for battle.\n那你也知道我们需要备战了。"

    old "Indeed. You need an army. I presume that's what brings you before me today."
    new "Indeed. You need an army. I presume that's what brings you before me today.\n不错。你们需要一支军队。我猜这就是你今天登门的原因。"

    old "You are correct."
    new "You are correct.\n正是。"

    old "Well then, you've come to the right place. If there's one thing I possess, it's military connections."
    new "Well then, you've come to the right place. If there's one thing I possess, it's military connections.\n那么，你来对地方了。要说我有什么，那就是军方的人脉。"

    old "That being said, most of the best officers I know have their attention preoccupied at the moment with a matter of local politics."
    new "That being said, most of the best officers I know have their attention preoccupied at the moment with a matter of local politics.\n话虽如此，我认识的大多数优秀军官，眼下都被一桩地方政治事务缠住了心神。"

    old "The monument on the hill?"
    new "The monument on the hill?\n山上的那座纪念碑？"

    old "So you are aware. Yes, I speak of The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier."
    new "So you are aware. Yes, I speak of The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier.\n看来你已知晓。没错，我说的就是 Tomb of the Unknown Soldier。"

    old "Do you need me to spell out the significance of that monument?"
    new "Do you need me to spell out the significance of that monument?\n需要我把那座纪念碑的意义细细道来吗？"

    old "I'm not sure that I need you to tell me, but I'd like to hear what you have to say all the same."
    new "I'm not sure that I need you to tell me, but I'd like to hear what you have to say all the same.\n我不确定是否需要你来讲，但我还是想听听你的说法。"

    old "As you might conclude from the title, in that tomb rests a soldier. His name and family are unknown. But the fact that we can't know him by name doesn't diminish his service to his fellow countrymen."
    new "As you might conclude from the title, in that tomb rests a soldier. His name and family are unknown. But the fact that we can't know him by name doesn't diminish his service to his fellow countrymen.\n从名字你大概也能猜到，那座墓里安息着一名士兵。他的姓名和家人都不为人知。但无法知其姓名，并不减损他对同胞的付出。"

    old "The tomb is much more than a burial chamber for a single man. It stands as a symbol, in recognition of the many unidentified countless men who have fallen in battle. We can't carve out tombstones for men whose names we do not know. The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier serves as a collective monument, to the memories of all who deserve recognition for their sacrifice."
    new "The tomb is much more than a burial chamber for a single man. It stands as a symbol, in recognition of the many unidentified countless men who have fallen in battle. We can't carve out tombstones for men whose names we do not know. The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier serves as a collective monument, to the memories of all who deserve recognition for their sacrifice.\n这座墓远不止是某个人的墓室。它是一座象征，用以纪念无数在战场上倒下的无名者。我们无法为不知其名的人刻碑立传。Tomb of the Unknown Soldier 就是一座集体纪念碑，铭记所有配得上为其牺牲而受表彰的人们。"

    old "No need. That monument is known well to citizens across the land."
    new "No need. That monument is known well to citizens across the land.\n不必了。那座纪念碑，全国各地的百姓都耳熟能详。"

    old "So I'm sure you understand why military men such as myself would believe so strongly in the sanctity of that monument."
    new "So I'm sure you understand why military men such as myself would believe so strongly in the sanctity of that monument.\n所以我想，你一定明白为什么像我这样的军人，会如此笃信那座纪念碑的神圣。"

    old "My understanding is that the a certain metalworkers guild would like that space to operate a steel smithy."
    new "My understanding is that the a certain metalworkers guild would like that space to operate a steel smithy.\n据我了解，某个金属工匠行会想用那块地经营一座炼钢工坊。"

    old "Indeed. Did Lady Geraldine inform you of the specifics of what the workers want?"
    new "Indeed. Did Lady Geraldine inform you of the specifics of what the workers want?\n不错。Geraldine 夫人可曾告诉你，那些工人究竟想要什么？"

    old "For the most part, yes."
    new "For the most part, yes.\n大体上说了。"

    old "I am guessing she made the argument that the metalworkers needed that space so that they could enjoy better working conditions. Is that the main argument she made?"
    new "I am guessing she made the argument that the metalworkers needed that space so that they could enjoy better working conditions. Is that the main argument she made?\n我猜，她提出的理由是，金属工匠需要那块地方，好享有更好的工作条件。这是她的主要论点吗？"

    old "Yes, she said as much."
    new "Yes, she said as much.\n是的，她是这么说的。"

    old "Did she tell you that she's the one that encouraged them to collectively strike as well?"
    new "Did she tell you that she's the one that encouraged them to collectively strike as well?\n她有没有告诉你，鼓励他们集体罢工的，也正是她本人？"

    old "That, she did not tell me."
    new "That, she did not tell me.\n这她倒没告诉我。"

    old "Well, she did. The metalworkers are striking because Geraldine encouraged it, and gave them certain assurances that they could be guaranteed enough funding to live on for the duration of the strike."
    new "Well, she did. The metalworkers are striking because Geraldine encouraged it, and gave them certain assurances that they could be guaranteed enough funding to live on for the duration of the strike.\n可她确实做了。金属工匠们罢工，是因为 Geraldine 从中鼓动，还向他们做了某种保证，担保他们在罢工期间有足够的资金维生。"

    old "I suppose now you may be wondering why it is that Geraldine encouraged them to strike."
    new "I suppose now you may be wondering why it is that Geraldine encouraged them to strike.\n我猜你现在可能纳闷，Geraldine 为何要鼓动他们罢工。"

    old "The thought had crossed my mind."
    new "The thought had crossed my mind.\n这个念头确实在我脑中闪过。"

    old "The truth is, Geraldine stands to gain from the metalworkers strike, if their demands are met. They intend to buy up that land and set up a new workshop, with capital provided by Geraldine. She will own a large stake in the ensuing enterprise."
    new "The truth is, Geraldine stands to gain from the metalworkers strike, if their demands are met. They intend to buy up that land and set up a new workshop, with capital provided by Geraldine. She will own a large stake in the ensuing enterprise.\n真相是，只要金属工匠们的要求得到满足，Geraldine 就能从中获利。他们打算买下那块地，建起一座新工坊，资金由 Geraldine 提供。她将在这家随之诞生的企业中握有大量股份。"

    old "Geraldine is trying to create an unbroken supply chain along that river that allows her to control every part of the weapons' creation, from the extraction of the steel to the export of the finished product."
    new "Geraldine is trying to create an unbroken supply chain along that river that allows her to control every part of the weapons' creation, from the extraction of the steel to the export of the finished product.\nGeraldine 正试图沿着那条河打造一条环环相扣的供应链，好让她掌控武器生产的每一个环节——从钢材的开采，到成品的出口。"

    old "Geraldine likes to talk about matters of social equality, but look at the wealth she's accumulated for herself. Don't let her fool you into thinking that anything she does is selfless."
    new "Geraldine likes to talk about matters of social equality, but look at the wealth she's accumulated for herself. Don't let her fool you into thinking that anything she does is selfless.\nGeraldine 喜欢把社会平等挂在嘴边，可看看她为自己积攒的财富吧。别让她蒙骗了你，以为她做的任何事都是无私的。"

    old "The metalworkers could build that new workshop anywhere. It's hardly the only hill with the same wind conditions. But Geraldine wanted to maximize profitability by integrating the workshop with the rest of her supply chain, so she had to pick the hill nearest to the river."
    new "The metalworkers could build that new workshop anywhere. It's hardly the only hill with the same wind conditions. But Geraldine wanted to maximize profitability by integrating the workshop with the rest of her supply chain, so she had to pick the hill nearest to the river.\n金属工匠们在哪儿都能建新工坊。具备相同通风条件的山丘又不止那一座。但 Geraldine 想把工坊与她供应链的其余部分整合起来，以谋取最大利润，所以她只能选离河最近的那座山。"

    old "Knowing that now, I hope you'll join me in opposing Geraldine's plans. Please, help me, and the other veterans, preserve the monument. I ensure you that we'll make it worth your while."
    new "Knowing that now, I hope you'll join me in opposing Geraldine's plans. Please, help me, and the other veterans, preserve the monument. I ensure you that we'll make it worth your while.\n如今你既已知情，我希望你能与我一道反对 Geraldine 的计划。请帮帮我，也帮帮其他退伍军人，保住这座纪念碑。我向你保证，我们定不让你白费力气。"

    old "I'm sorry, but I can't commit to supporting you in this matter."
    new "I'm sorry, but I can't commit to supporting you in this matter.\n抱歉，但在这件事上，我无法承诺支持你。"

    old "Let me guess. Geraldine already made you an offer. One involving steel weapons."
    new "Let me guess. Geraldine already made you an offer. One involving steel weapons.\n让我猜猜。Geraldine 已经向你开出了条件。一份牵涉钢制武器的条件。"

    old "She did, yes."
    new "She did, yes.\n是的，她确实开了。"

    old "You think it's really in my best interest to side with you?"
    new "You think it's really in my best interest to side with you?\n你觉得站到你这边，真符合我的最佳利益吗？"

    old "Of course, I'm not naive enough to think that I'm the only one making you an offer. I know you already met with Geraldine. I presume she made you an offer. One involving steel weapons, if I had to guess."
    new "Of course, I'm not naive enough to think that I'm the only one making you an offer. I know you already met with Geraldine. I presume she made you an offer. One involving steel weapons, if I had to guess.\n当然，我还没天真到以为只有我一个人向你开条件。我知道你已经见过 Geraldine。我猜她向你开了价——如果要我猜，是份牵涉钢制武器的价码。"

    old "Yes, she did."
    new "Yes, she did.\n是的，她开了。"

    old "I understand. You're probably considering other offers. Geraldine, if she's the woman I know her to be, has probably tried to use steel weapons as a bargaining chip. Am I right?"
    new "I understand. You're probably considering other offers. Geraldine, if she's the woman I know her to be, has probably tried to use steel weapons as a bargaining chip. Am I right?\n我明白。你多半还在权衡其他条件。Geraldine，若她还是我认识的那个女人，八成已经想拿钢制武器当谈判筹码了。我说得对吗？"

    old "Well, you're not wrong."
    new "Well, you're not wrong.\n你倒没说错。"

    old "Did she give you her big spiel, about how her steel weapons are the greatest military technology ever conceived, and will be the deciding factor in any combat scenario? Did she tell you that iron weapons are flimsy mush compared to steel?"
    new "Did she give you her big spiel, about how her steel weapons are the greatest military technology ever conceived, and will be the deciding factor in any combat scenario? Did she tell you that iron weapons are flimsy mush compared to steel?\n她是不是又对你大吹大擂了一番，说她的钢制武器是有史以来最伟大的军事技术，在任何战斗局面中都将成为决定因素？她是不是跟你说，跟钢比起来，铁制武器软得像一滩烂泥？"

    old "She didn't word it that strongly, but yes, she spoke at length about the virtues of steel weapons."
    new "She didn't word it that strongly, but yes, she spoke at length about the virtues of steel weapons.\n她的措辞没这么夸张，但没错，她确实长篇大论地讲了钢制武器的种种优点。"

    old "I wouldn't be an honest man if I disputed that steel weapons are stronger than iron. But as a military man, I can tell you that weapons are not what wins battles. Soldiers win battles."
    new "I wouldn't be an honest man if I disputed that steel weapons are stronger than iron. But as a military man, I can tell you that weapons are not what wins battles. Soldiers win battles.\n我若否认钢制武器强于铁制，那就不是个诚实人了。但作为一个军人，我可以告诉你，打赢仗的不是武器，而是士兵。"

    old "I agree completely."
    new "I agree completely.\n我完全同意。"

    old "Of course you agree. 'Soldiers win battles.' It's practically a truism. You wouldn't expect it to be a controversial view to take. But there are those who think that replacing a sword that weighs five pounds with a sword that weighs three pounds is the key to victory."
    new "Of course you agree. 'Soldiers win battles.' It's practically a truism. You wouldn't expect it to be a controversial view to take. But there are those who think that replacing a sword that weighs five pounds with a sword that weighs three pounds is the key to victory.\n你当然会同意。‘士兵打赢仗’——这几乎是句老生常谈。谁都不会觉得这是种离经叛道的看法。但偏偏有人以为，把五磅重的剑换成三磅重的剑，就是取胜的关键。"

    old "I'm not denying that superior weapons provide an advantage in battle. But it's a small advantage compared to a man's battle sense."
    new "I'm not denying that superior weapons provide an advantage in battle. But it's a small advantage compared to a man's battle sense.\n我并不否认，更精良的武器能在战斗中带来优势。但与一个人的战斗意识相比，那只是微末的优势。"

    old "Of course soldiers win battles. But I'm not sure that I see your point."
    new "Of course soldiers win battles. But I'm not sure that I see your point.\n士兵打赢仗，这当然没错。但我不太明白你的用意。"

    old "Offer me a novice fighter with a steel blade, or a trained fighter with an iron blade, and I'll take the poorly-equipped veteran every time. If a man is skilled enough with his blade, even a bronze weapon will enough for him to kill."
    new "Offer me a novice fighter with a steel blade, or a trained fighter with an iron blade, and I'll take the poorly-equipped veteran every time. If a man is skilled enough with his blade, even a bronze weapon will enough for him to kill.\n给我一个持钢刃的新手，或一个持铁刃的老练战士，我每次都选那个装备简陋的老兵。一个人的剑术若足够精湛，哪怕给他一件青铜兵器，也足以取人性命。"

    old "You don't need the best weapons. What you need are weapons that are good enough. Iron may not be as strong as steel, but it will suffice for your needs. What you cannot compromise is training and leadership."
    new "You don't need the best weapons. What you need are weapons that are good enough. Iron may not be as strong as steel, but it will suffice for your needs. What you cannot compromise is training and leadership.\n你们不需要最好的武器。你们需要的是够用的武器。铁也许不如钢坚固，但足以满足需求。真正不能打折扣的，是训练和统率。"

    old "Grimoire is building an army. Tell me, who are your soldiers?"
    new "Grimoire is building an army. Tell me, who are your soldiers?\nGrimoire 正在组建军队。告诉我，你们的士兵都是什么人？"

    old "Any man on the street who's willing to hold a weapon is being conscripted to defend his home."
    new "Any man on the street who's willing to hold a weapon is being conscripted to defend his home.\n街头上任何愿意拿起武器的人，都被征召来保卫家园。"

    old "Cedric stabs at the air with his finger."
    new "Cedric stabs at the air with his finger.\nCedric 用手指朝空中戳了戳。"

    old "Precisely. You are going into battle with farmers, bakers, brick layers, and stone masons. What you need are trained fighters. I can provide the officers to train your men so that they know a pike from an entrenching tool. And those same officers will lead your men into battle, providing their tactical expertise in the moments when it matters most."
    new "Precisely. You are going into battle with farmers, bakers, brick layers, and stone masons. What you need are trained fighters. I can provide the officers to train your men so that they know a pike from an entrenching tool. And those same officers will lead your men into battle, providing their tactical expertise in the moments when it matters most.\n正是。你带着上战场的，是农夫、面包师、砌砖工和石匠。你们需要的是训练有素的战士。我可以提供军官来训练你的人，让他们分得清长矛和堑壕铲。而同样是这些军官，会率领你的人冲上战场，在最关键的关头贡献他们的战术专长。"

    old "I am a man of great influence, especially among those with military backgrounds. If I publicly voice my support of Grimoire in her hour of need, you'll have the veteran officers you need. What you pay them for their time will pale in comparison to the value that they have to offer."
    new "I am a man of great influence, especially among those with military backgrounds. If I publicly voice my support of Grimoire in her hour of need, you'll have the veteran officers you need. What you pay them for their time will pale in comparison to the value that they have to offer.\n我是个颇有影响力的人，尤其是在有军旅背景的人中间。若我在 Grimoire 危难之际公开声援，你就能得到所需的退伍军官。你付给他们时间的报酬，与他们所能提供的价值相比，实在微不足道。"

    old "I presume this support doesn't come without condition."
    new "I presume this support doesn't come without condition.\n我想这份支持不会没有条件。"

    old "If Geraldine succeeds in desecrating The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier, veterans will take it as a personal slight. And if it is known that she acted with your support, no military man will take your side, no matter what I tell them."
    new "If Geraldine succeeds in desecrating The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier, veterans will take it as a personal slight. And if it is known that she acted with your support, no military man will take your side, no matter what I tell them.\n如果 Geraldine 真成功亵渎了 Tomb of the Unknown Soldier，退伍军人们会把这视作对他们个人的羞辱。而若再被人得知，她的行动有你在背后撑腰，那么无论我对他们说什么，都不会有军人站到你这边。"

    old "I don't blame them."
    new "I don't blame them.\n我不怪他们。"

    old "I'm glad you can understand."
    new "I'm glad you can understand.\n很高兴你能理解。"

    old "The truth is, a symbol like the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier means more than a profit-minded woman like Geraldine could ever hope to understand. An officer realizes there are things more important than money. Loyalty. Duty. Honor. Those are the values that we prize above all else."
    new "The truth is, a symbol like the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier means more than a profit-minded woman like Geraldine could ever hope to understand. An officer realizes there are things more important than money. Loyalty. Duty. Honor. Those are the values that we prize above all else.\n事实是，像 Tomb of the Unknown Soldier 这样的象征，其意义远非 Geraldine 那样一心逐利的女人所能理解。一名军官深知，有些东西比金钱更重要。忠诚。职责。荣誉。这些才是我们最珍视的价值。"

    old "Those countless unknown soldiers who sacrificed their lives on the field of battle upheld their duty to us, to the bitter end. It's only fair that we pay them the respect they deserve. Take away that monument, and you give up honor. That's something you can't put a price on. It is, and will always be, more valuable than any benefit that might come from a new forge or workshop."
    new "Those countless unknown soldiers who sacrificed their lives on the field of battle upheld their duty to us, to the bitter end. It's only fair that we pay them the respect they deserve. Take away that monument, and you give up honor. That's something you can't put a price on. It is, and will always be, more valuable than any benefit that might come from a new forge or workshop.\n那些在战场上献出生命的无数无名士兵，至死恪守了对我们的职责。我们理应给予他们应得的尊重。拆掉那座纪念碑，就等于放弃荣誉。荣誉无法标价。它现在、将来也永远，比任何新熔炉或工坊可能带来的好处都更宝贵。"

    old "Let them build the forge someplace else. Another location may not be as ideal, as efficient or profitable, but it'll make do all the same."
    new "Let them build the forge someplace else. Another location may not be as ideal, as efficient or profitable, but it'll make do all the same.\n让他们到别处去建熔炉吧。换个地方也许没那么理想、没那么高效或赚钱，但照样能凑合着用。"

    old "That's not exactly a logical course of action."
    new "That's not exactly a logical course of action.\n这可不算是合乎逻辑的做法。"

    old "You assume that logic is of the utmost importance."
    new "You assume that logic is of the utmost importance.\n你认定逻辑至关重要。"

    old "I can tell you what does matter to those veterans. Loyalty. Duty. Honor. Those are the principles that our service is based on. And you should be grateful that the military officers you hope to gain as allies place those above pure logic."
    new "I can tell you what does matter to those veterans. Loyalty. Duty. Honor. Those are the principles that our service is based on. And you should be grateful that the military officers you hope to gain as allies place those above pure logic.\n我可以告诉你，对退伍军人们而言什么才重要。忠诚。职责。荣誉。这些是我们从军生涯所本的准则。而你应该庆幸，你所希望争取为盟友的那些军官，把这些看得比纯粹的逻辑更重。"

    old "Assisting Grimoire in her hour of need is not a logical course of action, my friend. For a retired officer residing in Lothark to his estate is a highly unreasonable act."
    new "Assisting Grimoire in her hour of need is not a logical course of action, my friend. For a retired officer residing in Lothark to his estate is a highly unreasonable act.\n在 Grimoire 危难之际出手相助，可不是合乎逻辑的做法，我的朋友。对一位安坐在 Lothark 宅邸里的退役军官来说，这实在是不理智之举。"

    old "No amount of argument or logic could convince him to leave the safety and comfort of his home to serve on the battlefield. No, he does this because he is loyal to his fellows, because he is compelled by duty, and because he prizes honor even over his own life."
    new "No amount of argument or logic could convince him to leave the safety and comfort of his home to serve on the battlefield. No, he does this because he is loyal to his fellows, because he is compelled by duty, and because he prizes honor even over his own life.\n再多的道理或逻辑，也无法说服他离开安全舒适的家园，去战场上效命。不，他这么做，是因为忠于同袍，因为为职责所驱，因为他把荣誉看得比自己的性命还重。"

    old "If you want the loyalty of these men, you must earn it. The question is, will you?"
    new "If you want the loyalty of these men, you must earn it. The question is, will you?\n你若想要这些人的忠诚，就得自己去挣。问题是，你肯吗？"

    old "I can spend as long as I like telling you what to do. Ultimately, it's your decision to make. I think I've said my piece. Go and do as you will. I pray that for your sake and the fate of Grimoire that you make the right decision."
    new "I can spend as long as I like telling you what to do. Ultimately, it's your decision to make. I think I've said my piece. Go and do as you will. I pray that for your sake and the fate of Grimoire that you make the right decision.\n我可以一直告诉你该怎么做。但归根结底，决定权在你。我想我已把话说完。去吧，按你的意愿行事。我祈祷，为了你，也为了 Grimoire 的命运，你能做出正确的决定。"

    old "Thank you for taking the time to meet with me, Apolimesho."
    new "Thank you for taking the time to meet with me, Apolimesho.\n感谢你抽出时间见我，Apolimesho。"

    old "Of course. You can always consider it flattery when you consult my wisdom on any matter."
    new "Of course. You can always consider it flattery when you consult my wisdom on any matter.\n不客气。无论何事，只要你来请教我的智慧，都尽可视作对我的恭维。"

    old "What is it that weighs on your mind, [protag]?"
    new "What is it that weighs on your mind, [protag]?\n是什么事压在你心头，[protag]？"

    old "I've spent some time meeting with several nobles in Lothark."
    new "I've spent some time meeting with several nobles in Lothark.\n我花了些时间，在 Lothark 会见了数位贵族。"

    old "Apolimesho nods."
    new "Apolimesho nods.\nApolimesho 点点头。"

    old "Worthy allies, capable of aiding our war effort. Your time in Lothark is well-spent."
    new "Worthy allies, capable of aiding our war effort. Your time in Lothark is well-spent.\n堪当大任的盟友，能助我方的战事一臂之力。你在 Lothark 的时间没有白费。"

    old "Several of them drew my attention to a matter that's currently before the council of Grimoire."
    new "Several of them drew my attention to a matter that's currently before the council of Grimoire.\n其中几位让我注意到一件眼下正摆在 Grimoire 议会面前的事务。"

    old "What would that matter be?"
    new "What would that matter be?\n那是什么事务？"

    old "The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier."
    new "The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier.\nTomb of the Unknown Soldier。"

    old "Ah. Yes, I'm aware."
    new "Ah. Yes, I'm aware.\n啊。是的，我知道。"

    old "What are your thoughts, [protag]?"
    new "What are your thoughts, [protag]?\n你怎么看，[protag]？"

    old "I think that the council should do what's right. This isn't something that can be boiled down to a simple analysis of costs and benefits. The council isn't in the business of profiteering. The council's greatest responsibility, above all else, is to do what is right."
    new "I think that the council should do what's right. This isn't something that can be boiled down to a simple analysis of costs and benefits. The council isn't in the business of profiteering. The council's greatest responsibility, above all else, is to do what is right.\n我认为议会该做正确之事。这事不能简单归结为成本与收益的算计。议会不干牟取暴利的勾当。议会最大的责任，高于一切的，就是行正确之事。"

    old "And what do you believe that is?"
    new "And what do you believe that is?\n那你认为什么是正确之事？"

    old "That monument was built for a reason. To honor the dead. Even more specifically, it was built to honor the dead and unknown, those who will never have there name etched on a tombstone. Leaving that monument is the least that we can do for those soldiers who gave their lives."
    new "That monument was built for a reason. To honor the dead. Even more specifically, it was built to honor the dead and unknown, those who will never have there name etched on a tombstone. Leaving that monument is the least that we can do for those soldiers who gave their lives.\n那座纪念碑的建立自有其理由——为纪念逝者。更确切地说，是为纪念那些无名逝者，那些名字永远不会刻上墓碑的人。保留那座纪念碑，是我们能为那些献出生命的士兵做的最起码的事。"

    old "We owe our success in battle to the workers who make the weapons that we carry. Those workers are now petitioning to be recognized and work in more favorable conditions. How can we say no to that? We can't let sentimentality to interfere with our ability to reward those who toil so hard for our collective success."
    new "We owe our success in battle to the workers who make the weapons that we carry. Those workers are now petitioning to be recognized and work in more favorable conditions. How can we say no to that? We can't let sentimentality to interfere with our ability to reward those who toil so hard for our collective success.\n我们在战场上的胜绩，要归功于制造我们手中武器的工人。如今这些工人请愿，希望得到认可、能在更优厚的条件下工作。我们怎能拒绝？我们不能让感情用事，妨碍我们去犒赏那些为集体成功而辛苦劳作的工人。"

    old "I don't know. It's a moral dilemma."
    new "I don't know. It's a moral dilemma.\n我不知道。这是个道德难题。"

    old "I have respect—immense respect, but probably still not enough—for the men who have given their lives in service to their fellow countrymen. The least that we can do is to honor their memory, but there are so many men who fall in battle and are never recognized for their sacrifice. It seems that we owe them at least that monument as a token of gratitude."
    new "I have respect—immense respect, but probably still not enough—for the men who have given their lives in service to their fellow countrymen. The least that we can do is to honor their memory, but there are so many men who fall in battle and are never recognized for their sacrifice. It seems that we owe them at least that monument as a token of gratitude.\n我对那些为同胞效命、献出生命的人满怀敬意——至深的敬意，但恐怕仍不够。我们至少能做的是缅怀他们，但还有那么多人在战斗中倒下，其牺牲从未得到承认。看来，我们至少该把那座纪念碑留给他们，作为感激的见证。"

    old "The metalworkers have valid complaints, however. Working in a forge is no pleasant task, and yet we ask some of our best and brightest workers to endure those conditions. They serve a critical role in our war effort. You can't fight a war without weapons. We owe those workers gratitude for their contributions, and to say we're grateful to them while denying them that opportunity for better working conditions seems hypocritical."
    new "The metalworkers have valid complaints, however. Working in a forge is no pleasant task, and yet we ask some of our best and brightest workers to endure those conditions. They serve a critical role in our war effort. You can't fight a war without weapons. We owe those workers gratitude for their contributions, and to say we're grateful to them while denying them that opportunity for better working conditions seems hypocritical.\n然而，金属工匠们的不满也确有道理。在熔炉边劳作并非易事，我们却要求最优秀、最杰出的一些工人去忍受那种条件。他们在我们的战事中起着关键作用。没有武器，就打不了仗。我们欠那些工人一份感激，而一边说着感激他们，一边又剥夺他们改善工作条件的机会，这似乎有些虚伪。"

    old "I think that the council should do what's best for the city and its people. That's its responsibility, that's why it exists."
    new "I think that the council should do what's best for the city and its people. That's its responsibility, that's why it exists.\n我认为议会该为这座城市及其人民谋取最大福祉。那是它的职责所在，也是它存在的理由。"

    old "The question, on its face, seems simple. What decision will produce the best outcome for Grimoire in this time of need? But in practice, I'm finding its not so simple."
    new "The question, on its face, seems simple. What decision will produce the best outcome for Grimoire in this time of need? But in practice, I'm finding its not so simple.\n这个问题，表面上看似乎简单。在这个艰难时刻，怎样的决定能给 Grimoire 带来最好的结果？但在现实中，我发现它并不那么简单。"

    old "Military veterans value the monument, for obvious reasons. Duty, honor, respect, and loyalty, those are all things that are baked into them. Clearing the monument to build a steel mill would be a great sign of disrespect to those that the monument was erected to honor. If we want their support, we need to preserve that monument."
    new "Military veterans value the monument, for obvious reasons. Duty, honor, respect, and loyalty, those are all things that are baked into them. Clearing the monument to build a steel mill would be a great sign of disrespect to those that the monument was erected to honor. If we want their support, we need to preserve that monument.\n退伍军人珍视那座纪念碑，原因显而易见。职责、荣誉、敬意与忠诚，这些都深植于他们心中。铲平纪念碑去建炼钢厂，是对纪念碑所纪念之人的莫大不敬。我们若想要他们的支持，就得保住那座纪念碑。"

    old "But the steel craftsman want that space for themselves, and if we give it to them, they could prove to be a great asset. Better weapons for our soldiers could make a difference."
    new "But the steel craftsman want that space for themselves, and if we give it to them, they could prove to be a great asset. Better weapons for our soldiers could make a difference.\n但炼钢工匠们想要那块地自用，而若我们给了他们，他们兴许能成为一大助力。给我们的士兵更精良的武器，也许真能扭转局面。"

    old "I feel like either way, I'm going to be missing out on an opportunity."
    new "I feel like either way, I'm going to be missing out on an opportunity.\n我觉得无论怎么选，我都会错失一个机会。"

    old "Life is filled with missed opportunities. Right now you're talking to me. But the time that you're spending talking to me could have been spent doing something else."
    new "Life is filled with missed opportunities. Right now you're talking to me. But the time that you're spending talking to me could have been spent doing something else.\n人生处处是错失的机会。此刻你在跟我说话。但你花在与我交谈上的时间，本可以用来做别的事。"

    old "You could be building stronger bonds with the people that you plan to march into battle with. Or you could have spent that time training yourself. But you chose to spoke to me, because you think that this is an important matter."
    new "You could be building stronger bonds with the people that you plan to march into battle with. Or you could have spent that time training yourself. But you chose to spoke to me, because you think that this is an important matter.\n你本可以与你计划并肩作战的人们加深情谊，也可以把时间花在自我训练上。但你选择与我交谈，因为你觉得这是件重要的事。"

    old "That is for you to decide. Whatever decision you make, it will be better for you than the one I would make, because if I made it, it would not be yours. Do you understand?"
    new "That is for you to decide. Whatever decision you make, it will be better for you than the one I would make, because if I made it, it would not be yours. Do you understand?\n这要由你来决定。无论你做出什么决定，都比我会做出的决定更适合你，因为那若是我的决定，便不是你的了。你明白吗？"

    old "I'm not sure that I do."
    new "I'm not sure that I do.\n我不太确定自己明白。"

    old "You are trying to weigh the value of one thing against another. You approach this like it is some kind of objective question. But different people value different things. The strength or weakness of a given decision is often in the eye of the beholder. That is why you must choose."
    new "You are trying to weigh the value of one thing against another. You approach this like it is some kind of objective question. But different people value different things. The strength or weakness of a given decision is often in the eye of the beholder. That is why you must choose.\n你试图权衡一件事与另一件事的价值。你把这当成某种客观问题来处理。但不同的人看重不同的东西。某个决定的优劣，往往取决于看待它的人。正因如此，你必须自己选择。"

    old "What I can tell you is that many of the Grimoire council members are predisposed toward one side or another on this issue, but they could easily be persuaded. You've already invested a great deal more effort and time in this matter than they have, and you've become quite a persuasive talker."
    new "What I can tell you is that many of the Grimoire council members are predisposed toward one side or another on this issue, but they could easily be persuaded. You've already invested a great deal more effort and time in this matter than they have, and you've become quite a persuasive talker.\n我能告诉你的是，Grimoire 议会的许多成员在这个问题上本就倾向某一方，但他们很容易被说服。你在这件事上投入的精力与时间已远胜于他们，而你也早已是位颇具说服力的说客。"

    old "I am guessing that your verbal talents would be sufficient to win the necessary number of votes over to either side."
    new "I am guessing that your verbal talents would be sufficient to win the necessary number of votes over to either side.\n我猜，你的口才足以把所需数量的选票争取到任何一方。"

    old "The question is, what side will you choose? You came here with that question for me, and the best I can do is pose it back to you. Do not endeavor what you believe other people will see as correct. Do what you believe is the best option. I don't believe this is a matter where you can choose wrongly."
    new "The question is, what side will you choose? You came here with that question for me, and the best I can do is pose it back to you. Do not endeavor what you believe other people will see as correct. Do what you believe is the best option. I don't believe this is a matter where you can choose wrongly.\n问题是，你会选择哪一边？你带着这个问题来问我，而我所能做的，就是把它抛还给你。别去强求你认为别人眼中正确的事，去做你认为最好的选择。我不认为这件事上有选错的余地。"

    old "When I must decide?"
    new "When I must decide?\n我何时必须做出决定？"

    old "The Council's next session is on day 70. There's time for you to prepare yourself. Good luck, [protag]. I do not envy your responsability."
    new "The Council's next session is on day 70. There's time for you to prepare yourself. Good luck, [protag]. I do not envy your responsability.\n议会下一次会议在第 70 天。你有时间做好准备。祝你好运，[protag]。我可真不羡慕你肩上的责任。"

    old "I find Apolimesho waiting for me at the door of the general assembly meeting."
    new "I find Apolimesho waiting for me at the door of the general assembly meeting.\n我发现 Apolimesho 在大会会场门口等我。"

    old "Apolimesho. Are you participating in the vote?"
    new "Apolimesho. Are you participating in the vote?\nApolimesho。你要参加投票吗？"

    old "No, I came simply to observe and consult. Those who aren't voting can still attend the meeting, and have their chance to try and persuade voting members of the assembly to go in a specific direction."
    new "No, I came simply to observe and consult. Those who aren't voting can still attend the meeting, and have their chance to try and persuade voting members of the assembly to go in a specific direction.\n不，我只是来旁观和提供咨询。不参与投票的人仍可列席会议，也有机会试着说服大会中投票的成员朝特定方向走。"

    old "Ah, so do you have any plans to try and persuade any of the voting members?"
    new "Ah, so do you have any plans to try and persuade any of the voting members?\n啊，那你有没有打算试着说服哪位投票成员？"

    old "No, I think it's best for me to stay out of this. Some of the voting members of Lothark's general assembly don't take too kindly to members of Grimoire's council, and if one of them holds a grudge against me, I fear that trying to persuade them in a particular direction might have the opposite effect."
    new "No, I think it's best for me to stay out of this. Some of the voting members of Lothark's general assembly don't take too kindly to members of Grimoire's council, and if one of them holds a grudge against me, I fear that trying to persuade them in a particular direction might have the opposite effect.\n不，我想我最好置身事外。Lothark 大会的一些投票成员对 Grimoire 议会的成员不太友善，若其中有人对我心怀芥蒂，我担心试图说服他们朝某个方向走，反而可能适得其反。"

    old "If there are members of the Lothark assembly who don't like the Grimoire council, then what chances do I have of persuading any of them?"
    new "If there are members of the Lothark assembly who don't like the Grimoire council, then what chances do I have of persuading any of them?\n既然 Lothark 大会里有人不喜欢 Grimoire 议会，那我还有几分把握能说服他们中的任何一个？"

    old "You may be a representative of the Grimoire council, but you are not a member. You are a freelancer, in a sense. A mercenary. You work for the council, but you are not part of it. And among the market-minded members of Lothark, a mercenary with no deep-lying loyalties is someone they can trust to be a bit more neutral."
    new "You may be a representative of the Grimoire council, but you are not a member. You are a freelancer, in a sense. A mercenary. You work for the council, but you are not part of it. And among the market-minded members of Lothark, a mercenary with no deep-lying loyalties is someone they can trust to be a bit more neutral.\n你或许是 Grimoire 议会的代表，却并非其成员。从某种意义上说，你是个自由人。一个雇佣兵。你为议会效力，却不属于议会。而在 Lothark 那些精于商道的成员看来，一个没有深厚忠诚的雇佣兵，反而是他们可以信任的更中立之人。"

    old "That's interesting. I think most people generally tend to discuss mercenaries, since they're known for their lack of loyalty and simply selling their services to the highest bidder. But I suppose that to a group of merchants, who decide everything based on finance, that kind of person might be the most predictable."
    new "That's interesting. I think most people generally tend to discuss mercenaries, since they're known for their lack of loyalty and simply selling their services to the highest bidder. But I suppose that to a group of merchants, who decide everything based on finance, that kind of person might be the most predictable.\n这倒有趣。我想大多数人通常提起雇佣兵，都会说他们毫无忠诚，只会把服务卖给出价最高的人。但我想，对一群凡事以钱财决断的商人来说，那种人或许是最容易预料的。"

    old "Exactly. Of course, not every member of the assembly is persuadable. Many of them have already made up their minds, or have vested business interests which would compel them to vote in a particular direction."
    new "Exactly. Of course, not every member of the assembly is persuadable. Many of them have already made up their minds, or have vested business interests which would compel them to vote in a particular direction.\n正是。当然，并非每位大会成员都能被说服。他们中许多人早已拿定主意，或有既得商业利益，迫使他们朝特定方向投票。"

    old "Still, a few of them may be convinced. And from what I understand, the vote is fairly split. A small handful of votes could be the deciding factor."
    new "Still, a few of them may be convinced. And from what I understand, the vote is fairly split. A small handful of votes could be the deciding factor.\n不过，其中有几位或许还能争取。而据我所知，选票相当胶着。区区几张票，也许就能左右结果。"

    old "That's why I'm here."
    new "That's why I'm here.\n这正是我来的原因。"

    old "By the way, I noticed that neither Geraldine or Cedric are here. That's a bit surprising."
    new "By the way, I noticed that neither Geraldine or Cedric are here. That's a bit surprising.\n顺带一提，我注意到 Geraldine 和 Cedric 都没到场。这倒有点出人意料。"

    old "They both probably wanted to avoid a confrontation. Cedric is probably avoiding Geraldine, and Geraldine is avoiding Cedric, and that would explain why neither of them are here."
    new "They both probably wanted to avoid a confrontation. Cedric is probably avoiding Geraldine, and Geraldine is avoiding Cedric, and that would explain why neither of them are here.\n他们俩多半都想避免正面交锋。Cedric 大概在躲 Geraldine，Geraldine 也在躲 Cedric，这就能解释为什么他俩都不在场了。"

    old "Aren't they going to vote, though?"
    new "Aren't they going to vote, though?\n可他们不投票吗？"

    old "They both cast their ballots early. They've already voted."
    new "They both cast their ballots early. They've already voted.\n他们俩都早早投了票。已经投过了。"

    old "That's allowed?"
    new "That's allowed?\n这也能行？"

    old "Technically, an absentee ballot is supposed to only be used in cases where the voter would have pressing circumstances that would prevent them from attending in person. But in a place like Lothark, a simple explanation like having a business meeting is considered a valid reason to miss a vote and cast an absentee ballot."
    new "Technically, an absentee ballot is supposed to only be used in cases where the voter would have pressing circumstances that would prevent them from attending in person. But in a place like Lothark, a simple explanation like having a business meeting is considered a valid reason to miss a vote and cast an absentee ballot.\n按规矩，缺席选票本该只用于选民确有要事、无法亲自出席的情形。但在 Lothark 这种地方，‘有场商务会议’这样简单的理由，就被视为缺席投票、投出缺席选票的正当理由了。"

    old "I'm surprised that more people haven't done the same thing, if it's so easy to miss the vote."
    new "I'm surprised that more people haven't done the same thing, if it's so easy to miss the vote.\n既然缺席投票这么容易，我倒惊讶没更多人照做。"

    old "Most people actually enjoy attending the live voting process, even though the ballots are cast secretly. It gives them an opportunity to meet potential new business partners, or share gossip. In Lothark, politics is something that often brings people together. Many people treat these events the same way they might a social engagement."
    new "Most people actually enjoy attending the live voting process, even though the ballots are cast secretly. It gives them an opportunity to meet potential new business partners, or share gossip. In Lothark, politics is something that often brings people together. Many people treat these events the same way they might a social engagement.\n其实大多数人挺享受亲临现场投票的过程，尽管选票是秘密投出的。这给了他们结识潜在新商业伙伴、或闲聊八卦的机会。在 Lothark，政治常常是让人们聚到一起的由头。许多人对待这类场合，就像对待社交应酬一样。"

    old "In that case, it probably won't be too difficult to insert myself into any conversations."
    new "In that case, it probably won't be too difficult to insert myself into any conversations.\n那样的话，我插进任何一场交谈，大概都不会太难。"

    old "My advice would be to concentrate on the louder and more influential voices in the room. You won't have time to talk to everyone, but there are a few key influencers who, if they were persuaded to join your side, could help to rally votes."
    new "My advice would be to concentrate on the louder and more influential voices in the room. You won't have time to talk to everyone, but there are a few key influencers who, if they were persuaded to join your side, could help to rally votes.\n我的建议是，把注意力集中在屋里声音最响、最有影响力的那些人身上。你没时间与每个人都谈，但其中有几位关键的意见领袖，若能说服他们站到你这边，就能帮忙拉来选票。"

    old "I'm afraid I don't really know who in the room would fit that description."
    new "I'm afraid I don't really know who in the room would fit that description.\n恐怕我不太清楚，屋里谁符合这样的描述。"

    old "Well, as much as I have a distaste for it, I've spent enough time engaged in politics that I hear gossip about who the most influential voices are. There are two names that come to mind: Samael and Astrid."
    new "Well, as much as I have a distaste for it, I've spent enough time engaged in politics that I hear gossip about who the most influential voices are. There are two names that come to mind: Samael and Astrid.\n这个嘛，尽管我厌恶政治，但我在政坛浸淫已久，也听了不少关于谁是最有影响力声音的闲话。我想到两个名字：Samael 和 Astrid。"

    old "Who are they?"
    new "Who are they?\n他们是谁？"

    old "Samael is an up-and-comer. Despite being very young, he has a gregarious personality that many people seem to find endearing, and he seems to have the right combination of energy and charisma to persuade people to a specific side."
    new "Samael is an up-and-comer. Despite being very young, he has a gregarious personality that many people seem to find endearing, and he seems to have the right combination of energy and charisma to persuade people to a specific side.\nSamael 是个后起之秀。他虽十分年轻，却生性热络，许多人似乎都觉得他讨喜。他似乎正好兼具精力与魅力，能说服人们倒向某一方。"

    old "Granted, people who have staunchly-rooted positions probably won't change their minds on Samael's suggestion, but a lot of voters aren't firmly committed, and those are the kinds of voters who would be most susceptible to his influence."
    new "Granted, people who have staunchly-rooted positions probably won't change their minds on Samael's suggestion, but a lot of voters aren't firmly committed, and those are the kinds of voters who would be most susceptible to his influence.\n当然，立场根深蒂固的人多半不会因 Samael 的提议而改弦更张，但许多选民并未死心塌地，而这些人最容易受他的影响。"

    old "What about Astrid?"
    new "What about Astrid?\n那 Astrid 呢？"

    old "Astrid is well-known as a savvy investor. Her strategic investments have brought her substantial wealth over the years, and many business-minded people pay attention to where she's placing her money, because betting against Astrid usually doesn't pay off."
    new "Astrid is well-known as a savvy investor. Her strategic investments have brought her substantial wealth over the years, and many business-minded people pay attention to where she's placing her money, because betting against Astrid usually doesn't pay off.\nAstrid 以精明的投资者而闻名。多年来，她的战略投资为她带来了可观财富，许多有商业头脑的人都关注她把钱投往何处，因为押注 Astrid 的反面通常讨不到好。"

    old "Because of how successful she's been in the business world, many people regard her as a guru, and most people assume that if Astrid supports a given position, it means that it will be good for the city's economy."
    new "Because of how successful she's been in the business world, many people regard her as a guru, and most people assume that if Astrid supports a given position, it means that it will be good for the city's economy.\n正因她在商界如此成功，许多人把她奉为权威，大多数人认定，只要 Astrid 支持某个立场，那就意味着对这座城市的经济有利。"

    old "That being said, Astrid is an investor who tends to take the long-term approach, so most of the people who listen to her are the patient sort who are willing to endure potential short-term losses in the hopes of future gains."
    new "That being said, Astrid is an investor who tends to take the long-term approach, so most of the people who listen to her are the patient sort who are willing to endure potential short-term losses in the hopes of future gains.\n话虽如此，Astrid 是位倾向于着眼长远的投资者，所以听她话的人，大多是那种肯忍受潜在短期损失、以博取未来收益的耐心之人。"

    old "I see. Well, in that case, I suppose I should go and talk to:"
    new "I see. Well, in that case, I suppose I should go and talk to:\n我明白了。那么，我想我该去和……谈谈："

    old "I spot Astrid sitting in a corner alone. Her face appears to be buried in some sort of book. As I get closer, I see that it's not a book that she's reading, but a log of some kind, as the pages are filled with numbers of some sort. Upon seeing me approach, she snaps the logbook shut."
    new "I spot Astrid sitting in a corner alone. Her face appears to be buried in some sort of book. As I get closer, I see that it's not a book that she's reading, but a log of some kind, as the pages are filled with numbers of some sort. Upon seeing me approach, she snaps the logbook shut.\n我瞧见 Astrid 独自坐在角落里。她的脸似乎埋在某本书里。等我走近，才发现她看的不是书，而是某种账册，纸页上密密麻麻全是数字。一见我走近，她便啪地合上了账本。"

    old "My, my. Are you the Envoy of Grimoire?"
    new "My, my. Are you the Envoy of Grimoire?\n哎哟，哎呀。你就是 Grimoire 的特使吧？"

    old "Yes. How did you know?"
    new "Yes. How did you know?\n正是。你怎么知道？"

    old "I saw you talking with Apolimesho earlier. And you're the only face here I don't recognize."
    new "I saw you talking with Apolimesho earlier. And you're the only face here I don't recognize.\n我刚才瞧见你和 Apolimesho 说话。而你是这屋里我唯一认不得的面孔。"

    old "I'm actually glad you came to talk to me. I assume you're here because you have an opinion on the vote that's about to happen."
    new "I'm actually glad you came to talk to me. I assume you're here because you have an opinion on the vote that's about to happen.\n你来找我谈，其实我挺高兴。我猜你来，是因为对即将进行的投票有看法。"

    old "Cedric and Geraldine butting heads."
    new "Cedric and Geraldine butting heads.\nCedric 和 Geraldine 针锋相对。"

    old "I'm not so concerned with the individuals. For me, it's a simple case of making a rational decision: should the metalworkers have the hill? Or should it be left as a memorial?"
    new "I'm not so concerned with the individuals. For me, it's a simple case of making a rational decision: should the metalworkers have the hill? Or should it be left as a memorial?\n我关心的不是具体的人。对我来说，这只是个理性决断的问题：金属工匠该得到那座山吗？还是该把它留作纪念碑？"

    old "When I first approached this topic, the choice seemed obvious to me. Of course the metalworkers would make better use of the space. However, I have been studying enlistment logs for the past several decades."
    new "When I first approached this topic, the choice seemed obvious to me. Of course the metalworkers would make better use of the space. However, I have been studying enlistment logs for the past several decades.\n我最初接触这个话题时，选择似乎显而易见。金属工匠当然能把那片地方用得更好。然而，过去几十年我一直在研究征兵记录。"

    old "And I've noticed that in years when there were events in some way recognizing the military, such as ceremonies honoring individuals who served, an increased number of people chose to enlist. The same was true of events like the raising of a statue or the establishment of a landmark to recognize someone who provided valuable service."
    new "And I've noticed that in years when there were events in some way recognizing the military, such as ceremonies honoring individuals who served, an increased number of people chose to enlist. The same was true of events like the raising of a statue or the establishment of a landmark to recognize someone who provided valuable service.\n而我注意到，凡有以某种方式表彰军队的年份——比如为服役者举办致敬仪式——选择参军的人数就会增加。像为立下功勋者竖立雕像、或设立地标之类的事，也是如此。"

    old "Granted, the difference is small. Maybe a few percentage points per year. But when you compound that over ten or twenty years, it has a noticeable effect. As a long-term investor, I do best when things are stable, and a defense force that is consistently and steadily growing is highly conducive to that."
    new "Granted, the difference is small. Maybe a few percentage points per year. But when you compound that over ten or twenty years, it has a noticeable effect. As a long-term investor, I do best when things are stable, and a defense force that is consistently and steadily growing is highly conducive to that.\n当然，差异很小，也许每年只有几个百分点。但把这份差异复利累积十年、二十年，效果就颇为可观了。作为长线投资者，时局稳定时我最为得利，而一支持续稳步壮大的国防力量，正大有利于此。"

    old "On the other hand...there are numerous benefits of having a more productive metalworkers union. It has been a difficult choice to make."
    new "On the other hand...there are numerous benefits of having a more productive metalworkers union. It has been a difficult choice to make.\n而另一方面……拥有一个更高效的金属工匠行会，好处也着实不少。这真是个艰难的选择。"

    old "And compounding the issue is the fact that it seems incredibly difficult to get an informed, unbiased opinion on this issue. As much as I might respect Cedric and Geraldine, everything they say must be taken with a grain of salt. Cedric's own emotional ties to the memorial of course make him biased, and Geraldine serves her own self-interests by supporting the metalworkers. So, I've been waiting for an impartial observer to talk to."
    new "And compounding the issue is the fact that it seems incredibly difficult to get an informed, unbiased opinion on this issue. As much as I might respect Cedric and Geraldine, everything they say must be taken with a grain of salt. Cedric's own emotional ties to the memorial of course make him biased, and Geraldine serves her own self-interests by supporting the metalworkers. So, I've been waiting for an impartial observer to talk to.\n让问题更棘手的是，在这件事上，似乎极难得到一个知情而又不带偏见的意见。尽管我敬重 Cedric 和 Geraldine，但他们说的话都须打个折扣。Cedric 与那座纪念碑的情感羁绊自然使他有了偏向，而 Geraldine 支持金属工匠，则是为了一己私利。所以，我一直在等一位公正的旁观者，好与之谈谈。"

    old "You think I'm an impartial observer?"
    new "You think I'm an impartial observer?\n你觉得我是公正的旁观者？"

    old "You're not emotionally involved with the military the same way Cedric is, and you don't have a business interest like Geraldine does. Above all, your goal seems to be promoting the welfare of the Empire, does it not?"
    new "You're not emotionally involved with the military the same way Cedric is, and you don't have a business interest like Geraldine does. Above all, your goal seems to be promoting the welfare of the Empire, does it not?\n你不像 Cedric 那样与军方有情感瓜葛，也没有 Geraldine 那样的商业利益。最重要的是，你的目标似乎是促进帝国的福祉，不是吗？"

    old "And unlike all of the council members, who are part of voting factions and endlessly mired in politics, you seem to call things mostly as you see them. Obviously, not everything that comes out of your mouth is infallible, but at least I can expect you to be honest."
    new "And unlike all of the council members, who are part of voting factions and endlessly mired in politics, you seem to call things mostly as you see them. Obviously, not everything that comes out of your mouth is infallible, but at least I can expect you to be honest.\n而与所有议员不同——他们身处投票派系，又深陷政治泥潭——你似乎大多是照直说事。当然，你口中说出的并非句句无误，但至少我能指望你诚实。"

    old "So, tell me. Which do you think I should vote for? The metalworkers, or the veterans' memorial?"
    new "So, tell me. Which do you think I should vote for? The metalworkers, or the veterans' memorial?\n那么，告诉我。你觉得我该投哪边？金属工匠，还是退伍军人的纪念碑？"

    old "I think you should support the metalworkers."
    new "I think you should support the metalworkers.\n我觉得你该支持金属工匠。"

    old "Interesting. Why do you think that?"
    new "Interesting. Why do you think that?\n有意思。你为什么这么想？"

    old "Quite simply, investing in production means investing in the development of new technology."
    new "Quite simply, investing in production means investing in the development of new technology.\n很简单，投资生产，就等于投资新技术的发展。"

    old "Today, it means steel weapons. But lest we forget, the forging of steel weapons is something that was discovered by craftsmen who had the ability to tinker and experiment. The workshop will be a place where today's techniques are applied, but it's also a place where tomorrow's techniques will be developed."
    new "Today, it means steel weapons. But lest we forget, the forging of steel weapons is something that was discovered by craftsmen who had the ability to tinker and experiment. The workshop will be a place where today's techniques are applied, but it's also a place where tomorrow's techniques will be developed.\n今天，它意味着钢制武器。但别忘了，钢制武器的锻造，是那些有本事摆弄试验的工匠们发现的。这座工坊，既会是一处应用今日技艺的地方，也会是一处开发明日技艺的地方。"

    old "Of course, the steel weapons will be helpful in the conflict that the Empire is currently engaged in. But the value of the workshop goes far beyond that."
    new "Of course, the steel weapons will be helpful in the conflict that the Empire is currently engaged in. But the value of the workshop goes far beyond that.\n当然，钢制武器对帝国目前卷入的冲突会大有帮助。但这座工坊的价值远不止于此。"

    old "That is a very good point, [protag]. I have always considered new technologies to be the greatest source of opportunity. Who knows what new benefits we could reap over the years by dedicating resources to the refining of metalworking techniques?"
    new "That is a very good point, [protag]. I have always considered new technologies to be the greatest source of opportunity. Who knows what new benefits we could reap over the years by dedicating resources to the refining of metalworking techniques?\n这一点说得极好，[protag]。我一向认为，新技术是机遇的最大源泉。谁知道年复一年，我们投入资源去精进金属加工技艺，会收获怎样崭新的好处？"

    old "Whatever discoveries are made here could eventually travel outside of that workshop and be shared with other metalworkers around the empire."
    new "Whatever discoveries are made here could eventually travel outside of that workshop and be shared with other metalworkers around the empire.\n无论这里诞生了什么发现，最终都可能走出那座工坊，与帝国各地其他金属工匠分享。"

    old "Metalworkers are skilled laborers. Why allow their progress to be stymied by less-than-ideal working conditions?"
    new "Metalworkers are skilled laborers. Why allow their progress to be stymied by less-than-ideal working conditions?\n金属工匠是熟练的劳动者。为什么要让不尽如人意的工作条件阻碍他们的进步？"

    old "Yes, I had thought about that myself. But as I mentioned before, there are material benefits to that side. The benefit of the hill to the metalworkers may be easier to quantify, but it's not the only potential benefit that the hill could have."
    new "Yes, I had thought about that myself. But as I mentioned before, there are material benefits to that side. The benefit of the hill to the metalworkers may be easier to quantify, but it's not the only potential benefit that the hill could have.\n是的，我自己也想过这一点。但正如我之前所说，那一边也有实实在在的好处。山丘对金属工匠的好处也许更易量化，但那并非山丘可能带来的唯一好处。"

    old "I don't see it that way. It's really about giving people the best tools. About giving the metalworkers the best conditions for forging new weapons. And, as a consequence, giving soldiers the best weapons to march into battle with."
    new "I don't see it that way. It's really about giving people the best tools. About giving the metalworkers the best conditions for forging new weapons. And, as a consequence, giving soldiers the best weapons to march into battle with.\n我不这么看。说到底，这是给人们最好的工具，给金属工匠锻造新武器的最佳条件，进而给士兵们上战场时最好的武器。"

    old "I see what you're saying. But the memorial site has usefulness to society, as well. As much as I'm not one for sentimentality, I can't deny the effect that it has on people's behavior."
    new "I see what you're saying. But the memorial site has usefulness to society, as well. As much as I'm not one for sentimentality, I can't deny the effect that it has on people's behavior.\n我明白你的意思。但那处纪念地对社会也有用处。我虽不是个多愁善感的人，却也无法否认它对人们行为产生的影响。"

    old "Of course, there are multiple factors to consider."
    new "Of course, there are multiple factors to consider.\n当然，要考虑的因素不止一个。"

    old "I think you should vote for the veterans' memorial."
    new "I think you should vote for the veterans' memorial.\n我觉得你该投票支持退伍军人的纪念碑。"

    old "Sentimentality is a valuable resource. I know it sounds a bit cynical to phrase it like that, but if you treat it like a cost-benefit analysis, one of the things you have to consider when evaluating the value of something is considering how much it would cost to replace it."
    new "Sentimentality is a valuable resource. I know it sounds a bit cynical to phrase it like that, but if you treat it like a cost-benefit analysis, one of the things you have to consider when evaluating the value of something is considering how much it would cost to replace it.\n情感是种宝贵的资源。我知道这样说听起来有些冷嘲热讽，但若你把它当作成本收益分析，那么在评估一件东西的价值时，必须考虑的一项，就是替换它需要付出多少代价。"

    old "Finding a good place to install a workshop might be a challenging task. It's all about location, and what's ideal for integrating into a supply chain. But the fact is that workshops like that can be built quickly and get up to full production within a matter of weeks."
    new "Finding a good place to install a workshop might be a challenging task. It's all about location, and what's ideal for integrating into a supply chain. But the fact is that workshops like that can be built quickly and get up to full production within a matter of weeks.\n找一处好地方建工坊，或许是件费劲的事。关键在于选址，以及什么位置最适合融入供应链。但事实是，那样的工坊可以很快建成，几周之内就能满负荷生产。"

    old "A memorial like the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier, on the other hand...part of the value of that landmark is its age. That kind of value is built up slowly, over time. Unlike a workshop that scales up to full production in a matter of weeks, a memorial or landmark is something that can take years or even decade to accrue and fully realize its value."
    new "A memorial like the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier, on the other hand...part of the value of that landmark is its age. That kind of value is built up slowly, over time. Unlike a workshop that scales up to full production in a matter of weeks, a memorial or landmark is something that can take years or even decade to accrue and fully realize its value.\n而像 Tomb of the Unknown Soldier 这样的纪念碑……其价值一部分正在于它的年岁。那种价值是随时间缓慢累积的。与几周内就能扩产到满负荷的工坊不同，一处纪念碑或地标，需要数年甚至十年，才能积累并充分实现其价值。"

    old "That is a very good point, [protag]. There are certain assets that are more fungible than others, and landmarks that have sentimentality may be the least fungible of all resources. They have a value that's very difficult to replicate."
    new "That is a very good point, [protag]. There are certain assets that are more fungible than others, and landmarks that have sentimentality may be the least fungible of all resources. They have a value that's very difficult to replicate.\n这一点说得极好，[protag]。有些资产比其他资产更易替代，而承载情感的地标，或许是所有资源中最难替代的。它们的价值极难复制。"

    old "A lot of people are going to be upset if the memorial is removed. And an unhappy populace is not a productive populace."
    new "A lot of people are going to be upset if the memorial is removed. And an unhappy populace is not a productive populace.\n若纪念碑被拆除，许多人都会不满。而心怀不满的民众，不会是高效的民众。"

    old "Hmm. Do you think it would upset that many people?"
    new "Hmm. Do you think it would upset that many people?\n嗯。你觉得会惹恼那么多人吗？"

    old "What's important isn't how many people it upsets so much as who it upsets. Think about it. The people who are least committed to the nation's defense probably don't care very much about the memorial. The people who are most dedicated to the Empire's defense may end up caring a great deal. Which group of people do you think matters more?"
    new "What's important isn't how many people it upsets so much as who it upsets. Think about it. The people who are least committed to the nation's defense probably don't care very much about the memorial. The people who are most dedicated to the Empire's defense may end up caring a great deal. Which group of people do you think matters more?\n重要的不是惹恼多少人，而是惹恼了谁。想想看。最不关心国防的人，大概也不怎么在乎那座纪念碑。而对帝国防务最尽心的人，可能会非常在乎。你觉得哪群人更要紧？"

    old "Point taken. But the degree to which someone cares is not necessarily a measure of the degree to which they contribute to society. It is tricky to consider."
    new "Point taken. But the degree to which someone cares is not necessarily a measure of the degree to which they contribute to society. It is tricky to consider.\n言之有理。但一个人在乎的程度，未必能衡量他对社会的贡献程度。这一点颇难斟酌。"

    old "Astrid opens her logbook to a blank page and begins scribbling some notes, perhaps inspired by what I just said, or perhaps writing down something she just thought of. Her writing is too messy for me to make sense of it."
    new "Astrid opens her logbook to a blank page and begins scribbling some notes, perhaps inspired by what I just said, or perhaps writing down something she just thought of. Her writing is too messy for me to make sense of it.\nAstrid 把账本翻到一页空白，开始匆匆记下几笔——也许是受我刚才那番话的启发，也许只是记下她刚想到的事。她的字迹太过潦草，我瞧不出写的什么。"

    old "Thank you for your input, [protag]. I will certainly consider it."
    new "Thank you for your input, [protag]. I will certainly consider it.\n谢谢你的意见，[protag]。我一定会认真考虑。"

    old "I spot Samael in a corner, talking in a loud and animated fashion to three people who are listening with rapt attention. Eventually, he reaches the end of his story, and they begin laughing. Amidst their laugher, Samael seems to notice me, and he breaks away from the group chat and walks up to me."
    new "I spot Samael in a corner, talking in a loud and animated fashion to three people who are listening with rapt attention. Eventually, he reaches the end of his story, and they begin laughing. Amidst their laugher, Samael seems to notice me, and he breaks away from the group chat and walks up to me.\n我瞧见 Samael 在角落里，正声情并茂地对三个聚精会神的听众高谈阔论。最终，他的故事讲到了头，那几人笑了起来。在笑声中，Samael 似乎注意到了我，他从那群人里脱身，朝我走来。"

    old "Hello there. I'm Samael. You're [protag], right?"
    new "Hello there. I'm Samael. You're [protag], right?\n你好呀。我是 Samael。你是 [protag]，对吧？"

    old "Yes. I'm surprised you already know my name."
    new "Yes. I'm surprised you already know my name.\n是的。你居然已经知道我的名字，真叫我意外。"

    old "I make it a point to learn everyone's name. I'll admit, I can be a forgetful person, but I have a real knack for remembering people's names!"
    new "I make it a point to learn everyone's name. I'll admit, I can be a forgetful person, but I have a real knack for remembering people's names!\n我向来把记下每个人的名字当作要事。我承认，我这人挺健忘，但唯独记人名，我可是真有一手！"

    old "You learn people's names, even when you haven't met them already?"
    new "You learn people's names, even when you haven't met them already?\n你连还没见过面的人的名字都能记住？"

    old "Well, not everyone's names. It's a big city, and my memory isn't good enough to remember the names of every man, woman, and child who walks the streets. But you, you're something special, [protag]! And that's why I'm so glad I got a chance to talk to you."
    new "Well, not everyone's names. It's a big city, and my memory isn't good enough to remember the names of every man, woman, and child who walks the streets. But you, you're something special, [protag]! And that's why I'm so glad I got a chance to talk to you.\n这个嘛，也不是每个人的名字。这是座大城市，我的记性还没好到能记住街上每个男女老少的名字。但你，你可是个特别的人，[protag]！所以能有幸跟你聊聊，我真是太高兴了。"

    old "If Samael wants to talk to me, then perhaps this will be easier than I thought."
    new "If Samael wants to talk to me, then perhaps this will be easier than I thought.\n既然 Samael 想跟我谈，那也许这比我想象的容易。"

    old "Oh? Why's that?"
    new "Oh? Why's that?\n哦？怎么说？"

    old "To put it bluntly, I'm a bit undecided on this vote. You know, which side I should vote for. It seems to be a bit of a split vote between people who side with Cedric, and people who side with Geraldine. I don't really have close ties to either of them, so how am I supposed to make a decision?"
    new "To put it bluntly, I'm a bit undecided on this vote. You know, which side I should vote for. It seems to be a bit of a split vote between people who side with Cedric, and people who side with Geraldine. I don't really have close ties to either of them, so how am I supposed to make a decision?\n直说吧，这次投票我有点拿不定主意。你知道的，我该投哪一边。选票似乎分成了两派：一派站 Cedric，一派站 Geraldine。我跟他们俩都没什么深交，那我到底该怎么决定呢？"

    old "I thought you might give me a new perspective. Everyone I try talking to about these issues, it's the same talking points, over and over again. Everybody talks as if they think they have an original idea, but really they're not adding anything new to the discussion."
    new "I thought you might give me a new perspective. Everyone I try talking to about these issues, it's the same talking points, over and over again. Everybody talks as if they think they have an original idea, but really they're not adding anything new to the discussion.\n我原以为你或许能给我个新视角。我想找人谈谈这些事的每一个人，翻来覆去都是同一套说辞。人人都说得好像自己见解独到，其实根本没给讨论添什么新东西。"

    old "That's why I think it's helpful to get an outsider's perspective. How do you decide in a situation like this?"
    new "That's why I think it's helpful to get an outsider's perspective. How do you decide in a situation like this?\n所以我觉得，听听局外人的视角会有帮助。遇到这种情况，你会怎么决断？"

    old "I think you should focus on the people. True, you might not have any personal ties to either Geraldine or Cedric, but who do you admire more?"
    new "I think you should focus on the people. True, you might not have any personal ties to either Geraldine or Cedric, but who do you admire more?\n我觉得你该着眼于人本身。不错，你也许跟 Geraldine 或 Cedric 都没有私交，但你更敬慕谁？"

    old "Ah, that's a tough choice! On one hand, both of them have admirable qualities. Cedric's quite an honorable and respected man, but Geraldine is quite clever and shrewd with her business talents. On the other hand, I wonder if Cedric is a bit too caught up the old way of doing things, and Geraldine can be quite cutthroat when it comes to doing business."
    new "Ah, that's a tough choice! On one hand, both of them have admirable qualities. Cedric's quite an honorable and respected man, but Geraldine is quite clever and shrewd with her business talents. On the other hand, I wonder if Cedric is a bit too caught up the old way of doing things, and Geraldine can be quite cutthroat when it comes to doing business.\n啊，这可难选！一方面，他们俩都有值得敬慕的品格。Cedric 是位相当可敬、受人尊重的人，而 Geraldine 精明干练，商业才能出众。另一方面，我又觉得 Cedric 是不是太拘泥于老一套的做事方式，而 Geraldine 做起生意来，可是相当心狠手辣。"

    old "I think you should focus on the issue."
    new "I think you should focus on the issue.\n我觉得你该着眼于问题本身。"

    old "Hmm, you think so? To be honest, that was never really my strong suit. The reason I wanted to become a businessman isn't so that I could deal with numbers and logistics and counting money. It's really the people that I find interesting."
    new "Hmm, you think so? To be honest, that was never really my strong suit. The reason I wanted to become a businessman isn't so that I could deal with numbers and logistics and counting money. It's really the people that I find interesting.\n嗯，你这么觉得？说实话，那从来不是我的强项。我想当商人，不是为了跟数字、物流和数钱打交道。真正让我感兴趣的，是人。"

    old "Finding new business partners, meeting new people...why, I'm talking to you right now. It's conversations like these that are the real bread and butter of business, don't you think?"
    new "Finding new business partners, meeting new people...why, I'm talking to you right now. It's conversations like these that are the real bread and butter of business, don't you think?\n结识新的生意伙伴、遇见新的人……喏，我这不就在跟你说话嘛。像这样的交谈，才是生意的真正命脉，你不觉得吗？"

    old "I suppose so."
    new "I suppose so.\n我想是吧。"

    old "Be straight with me. If you had to side with one or the other, who would it be?"
    new "Be straight with me. If you had to side with one or the other, who would it be?\n跟我直说吧。若非得在他们俩之间选一边，你选谁？"

    old "Well, if you're asking me straight out, it would have to be..."
    new "Well, if you're asking me straight out, it would have to be...\n好吧，既然你开门见山地问，那就只能是……"

    old "Geraldine."
    new "Geraldine.\nGeraldine。"

    old "Oh? Why is that?"
    new "Oh? Why is that?\n哦？为什么？"

    old "Geraldine cares about the younger generation."
    new "Geraldine cares about the younger generation.\nGeraldine 关心年轻一代。"

    old "I haven't heard this argument. What do you mean, exactly?"
    new "I haven't heard this argument. What do you mean, exactly?\n这个论点我还没听过。你究竟是什么意思？"

    old "The real value of the war memorial is, well, sentimentality. It has value to veterans. People who have fought in years before. I'm not going to dispute that fact."
    new "The real value of the war memorial is, well, sentimentality. It has value to veterans. People who have fought in years before. I'm not going to dispute that fact.\n那座战争纪念碑的真正价值，说到底，是情感。它对退伍军人有价值，对那些多年前上过战场的人有价值。这个事实我不争辩。"

    old "But what about the younger generation? What about the people who haven't fought in battle before, but are going to march off for the first time? Don't you think that younger generation ought to be equipped with the best tools possible? It would give them the best chance of survival."
    new "But what about the younger generation? What about the people who haven't fought in battle before, but are going to march off for the first time? Don't you think that younger generation ought to be equipped with the best tools possible? It would give them the best chance of survival.\n但年轻一代呢？那些还没上过战场、却即将第一次出征的人呢？你不觉得年轻一代理应配备尽可能好的工具吗？那会给他们最大的生存机会。"

    old "True, but I think you're ignoring the value that veterans' experience could have to the younger generation."
    new "True, but I think you're ignoring the value that veterans' experience could have to the younger generation.\n不错，但我觉得你忽略了退伍军人的经验对年轻一代的价值。"

    old "Mentorship may be important, but ultimately most of what soldiers know, they learn by doing. And that learning process will be a lot easier and more productive if they have the best tools available. The next generation of soldiers doesn't need aging leadership lecturing them. What they need is a good solid weapon and some solid light armor."
    new "Mentorship may be important, but ultimately most of what soldiers know, they learn by doing. And that learning process will be a lot easier and more productive if they have the best tools available. The next generation of soldiers doesn't need aging leadership lecturing them. What they need is a good solid weapon and some solid light armor.\n言传身教固然重要，但归根结底，士兵所知的大半，都是在实战中学到的。而若他们拥有最好的工具，那个学习过程就会轻松得多、也高效得多。下一代士兵不需要年迈的长官对他们耳提面命。他们需要的，是一件扎实的好武器，和一身结实的轻甲。"

    old "So, you think that betting on Geraldine is betting on the future, the next generation of the Empire's military."
    new "So, you think that betting on Geraldine is betting on the future, the next generation of the Empire's military.\n所以，你认为押注 Geraldine，就是押注未来，押注帝国军队的下一代。"

    old "I wouldn't have thought about it that way, but I like the way you lay it out. It makes a lot of sense."
    new "I wouldn't have thought about it that way, but I like the way you lay it out. It makes a lot of sense.\n我本不会这么想，但我喜欢你这样讲。听来很有道理。"

    old "Geraldine wants to make sure that the city is making the best of what it has to offer."
    new "Geraldine wants to make sure that the city is making the best of what it has to offer.\nGeraldine 想确保这座城市能物尽其用，发挥出它所能提供的一切。"

    old "You're talking about resource allocation?"
    new "You're talking about resource allocation?\n你在说资源配置？"

    old "Well, yes. Geraldine is willing to look past people's feelings and look at what would really be the most useful thing to do with the memorial site. It's challenging the status quo, but you have to admire the way that she's so committed that she's willing to take on this issue."
    new "Well, yes. Geraldine is willing to look past people's feelings and look at what would really be the most useful thing to do with the memorial site. It's challenging the status quo, but you have to admire the way that she's so committed that she's willing to take on this issue.\n嗯，是的。Geraldine 愿意撇开人们的感受，去看那块纪念地真正最该派什么用场。这是在挑战现状，但你不得不钦佩她如此执着，竟愿意揽下这件事。"

    old "I suppose so. But Cedric is taking a stand, in his own way. Admittedly, he does represent the status quo, but it's not as if he's been entirely silent on this matter, either."
    new "I suppose so. But Cedric is taking a stand, in his own way. Admittedly, he does represent the status quo, but it's not as if he's been entirely silent on this matter, either.\n我想也是。但 Cedric 也以自己的方式表明了立场。诚然，他确实代表着现状，但在这件事上，他倒也没完全沉默。"

    old "Cedric."
    new "Cedric.\nCedric。"

    old "Siding with Cedric means siding with the courage and passion of veteran soldiers."
    new "Siding with Cedric means siding with the courage and passion of veteran soldiers.\n站在 Cedric 一边，就是站在退伍军人的勇气与热忱一边。"

    old "Interesting. Why do you think that matters?"
    new "Interesting. Why do you think that matters?\n有意思。你为什么觉得这很重要？"

    old "People aren't passionate over nothing. When you see a lot of passionate people on one side of an issue, a lot of people who are speaking and acting with conviction, that has to count for something, you know? There must be a reason that they're so passionate."
    new "People aren't passionate over nothing. When you see a lot of passionate people on one side of an issue, a lot of people who are speaking and acting with conviction, that has to count for something, you know? There must be a reason that they're so passionate.\n人们不会无缘无故地满怀热忱。当你看到一件事情的某一侧有那么多满怀热忱的人，那么多言之凿凿、行之以信念的人，那总该说明点什么，你知道吗？他们如此热忱，必有缘由。"

    old "I also put a lot of stock in people who have exhibited courage. It's not always easy to stand up for an unpopular position. A lot of people are silent about what they believe. So when someone like Cedric speaks out, I know he's doing it from a place of conviction, rather than going along with what might happen \"to be popular.\""
    new "I also put a lot of stock in people who have exhibited courage. It's not always easy to stand up for an unpopular position. A lot of people are silent about what they believe. So when someone like Cedric speaks out, I know he's doing it from a place of conviction, rather than going along with what might happen \"to be popular.\"\n我也很看重那些展现过勇气的人。为不受欢迎的立场挺身而出，并不总是易事。许多人对自己的信念沉默不语。所以，当 Cedric 这样的人发声时，我知道他是出于信念，而不是随波逐流去‘讨好大众’。"

    old "You make a good point, [protag]."
    new "You make a good point, [protag].\n你说得在理，[protag]。"

    old "Society owes a debt to men like Cedric."
    new "Society owes a debt to men like Cedric.\n社会亏欠 Cedric 这样的人一份情。"

    old "Those who perform military service risk their lives for the rest of us. When a man like Cedric tries to argue on behalf of those soldiers and former soldiers, we owe it to him to listen."
    new "Those who perform military service risk their lives for the rest of us. When a man like Cedric tries to argue on behalf of those soldiers and former soldiers, we owe it to him to listen.\n那些服兵役的人，为我们其余人甘冒生命危险。当 Cedric 这样的人试图为那些士兵和退伍士兵发声时，我们理当倾听。"

    old "Hmm, is that so? I guess I can see your perspective. Certainly I think it's important to hear him out. But that still leaves me with the question of whether he's better than the alternative. I wouldn't automatically support something said by someone like Cedric, you know?"
    new "Hmm, is that so? I guess I can see your perspective. Certainly I think it's important to hear him out. But that still leaves me with the question of whether he's better than the alternative. I wouldn't automatically support something said by someone like Cedric, you know?\n嗯，是这样吗？我想我能明白你的视角。当然，我认为倾听他的意见很重要。但这仍给我留下一个问题：他是否就胜过另一选择。我可不会只因为话出自 Cedric 这样的人物，就自动支持，你知道吗？"

    old "Several men walk up to Samael, and he turns and shakes hands with me."
    new "Several men walk up to Samael, and he turns and shakes hands with me.\n几个人朝 Samael 走来，他转过身，与我握了握手。"

    old "I'm afraid that's all the time I have. It was a pleasure talking to you, [protag]."
    new "I'm afraid that's all the time I have. It was a pleasure talking to you, [protag].\n恐怕我就只有这点时间了。与你交谈十分愉快，[protag]。"

    old "[protag]. Did you have a productive chat with the voting members?"
    new "[protag]. Did you have a productive chat with the voting members?\n[protag]。你和投票成员们谈得可有成效？"

    old "Perhaps. I suppose now all we can do is wait."
    new "Perhaps. I suppose now all we can do is wait.\n也许吧。我想现在我们也只能等待了。"

    old "Wait. I haven't voted yet. I was waiting for you, [protag]."
    new "Wait. I haven't voted yet. I was waiting for you, [protag].\n等等。我还没投票呢。我一直在等你，[protag]。"

    old "Me? Why?"
    new "Me? Why?\n我？为什么？"

    old "Who should I side with? Cedric or Geraldine?"
    new "Who should I side with? Cedric or Geraldine?\n我该站在哪一边？Cedric 还是 Geraldine？"

    old "You're not going to decide for yourself?"
    new "You're not going to decide for yourself?\n你不自己拿主意吗？"

    old "I trust your judgment more than anyone, [protag]. You're the only one who has no interest except doing a good job and saving us from the undead. Besides, I've trusted your judgment in many other matters before."
    new "I trust your judgment more than anyone, [protag]. You're the only one who has no interest except doing a good job and saving us from the undead. Besides, I've trusted your judgment in many other matters before.\n我比信任任何人都更信任你的判断，[protag]。你是唯一别无用心的人，只想把事情办好、把我们从亡灵手中解救出来。况且，我此前已在许多别的事情上信任过你的判断。"

    old "Well, thank you, Apolimesho."
    new "Well, thank you, Apolimesho.\n那么，谢谢你，Apolimesho。"

    old "So what it will be?"
    new "So what it will be?\n那么，你的决定是什么？"

    old "Even if Cedric and Geraldine aren't present, I'm pretty sure they've ears and eyes even in this room. I have the feeling that what I'll tell Apolimesho won't remain a secret."
    new "Even if Cedric and Geraldine aren't present, I'm pretty sure they've ears and eyes even in this room. I have the feeling that what I'll tell Apolimesho won't remain a secret.\n即便 Cedric 和 Geraldine 不在场，我也敢肯定，就连这屋里也有他们的耳目。我有种感觉，我要对 Apolimesho 说的话，不会成为秘密。"

    old "Apolimesho leaves me and goes to vote. He's one of the last to cast his vote, and though the ballots are supposed to be secret, I sense that eyes were on both me and Apolimesho, overhearing us as we spoke."
    new "Apolimesho leaves me and goes to vote. He's one of the last to cast his vote, and though the ballots are supposed to be secret, I sense that eyes were on both me and Apolimesho, overhearing us as we spoke.\nApolimesho 离开我，去投票了。他是最后投票的人之一，尽管选票本应是秘密的，我却感觉到，有目光落在我和 Apolimesho 两人身上，偷听着我们方才的谈话。"

    old "I sit back and watch as different members enter, each casting their secret ballot. Some people simply cast their vote and leave, while others stand around and gossip. After about half an hour, the voting is closed and the votes are tallied."
    new "I sit back and watch as different members enter, each casting their secret ballot. Some people simply cast their vote and leave, while others stand around and gossip. After about half an hour, the voting is closed and the votes are tallied.\n我往后一靠，看着不同的成员陆续进场，各自投下自己的秘密选票。有些人投完票便离开，还有些人留在原地闲谈八卦。约莫半小时后，投票结束，开始计票。"

    old "To those still present, thank you for coming today to vote. This was a close vote, and it's rare to see people so split on a topic, but it seems a number of people came at the last minute to voice their opinion."
    new "To those still present, thank you for coming today to vote. This was a close vote, and it's rare to see people so split on a topic, but it seems a number of people came at the last minute to voice their opinion.\n对仍在场的诸位，感谢你们今天前来投票。这是一次势均力敌的投票，很少见到人们在一个议题上如此分歧，不过，看来有不少人赶在最后一刻前来表达了自己的意见。"

    old "The resolution to approve the site of the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier as a location for the new workshop has been approved. Logistical details will follow as described in the initial resolution sponsored by Lady Geraldine."
    new "The resolution to approve the site of the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier as a location for the new workshop has been approved. Logistical details will follow as described in the initial resolution sponsored by Lady Geraldine.\n批准将 Tomb of the Unknown Soldier 所在地作为新工坊选址的决议已获通过。后续后勤细节，将依 Geraldine 夫人最初所提决议所述执行。"

    old "The resolution to replace the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier and appropriate it as a building site for a new workshop has failed to pass. This land will continue to serve its current function and no further building or development will be permitted at this site."
    new "The resolution to replace the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier and appropriate it as a building site for a new workshop has failed to pass. This land will continue to serve its current function and no further building or development will be permitted at this site.\n取代 Tomb of the Unknown Soldier、并将其划作新工坊建筑用地的决议未获通过。这片土地将继续维持其现有用途，此地将不再允许任何进一步的建造或开发。"

    old "The announcer at the ballot table goes on for several more minutes explaining several more details of the resolution, but by this point everyone seems to be leaving. Apolimesho walks up to me."
    new "The announcer at the ballot table goes on for several more minutes explaining several more details of the resolution, but by this point everyone seems to be leaving. Apolimesho walks up to me.\n计票台旁的宣读人又继续讲了几分钟，解说决议的更多细节，但此时众人似乎都已准备离场。Apolimesho 走到我面前。"

    old "Well, it looks like the vote has concluded. Apparently the final outcome was decided by just a few votes. I wonder if your persuasive words in the final moments leading up to the vote could have been what tipped the scale."
    new "Well, it looks like the vote has concluded. Apparently the final outcome was decided by just a few votes. I wonder if your persuasive words in the final moments leading up to the vote could have been what tipped the scale.\n那么，看来投票已经结束。最终结果显然只由寥寥几票决定。我在想，你在投票前最后关头那些颇具说服力的话，会不会正是扭转天平的关键。"

